t["subzone:razorwind-canyon"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,239,25.462.0,20.394.0,34.240.0,40.189.0,45.204.0,45.160.0",["h"]="7a0482",["n"]="Cañón del Ventajo",["s"]="Cañón del Ventajo. El Cañón del Ventajo es un barranco rocoso y serpenteante dividido a través del camino principal entre Cerrotajo y Orgrimmar. Infestado por las agresivas arpías Dustwind, el cañón representa un peligro constante para los viajeros que avanzan hacia el norte, rumbo a la capital de la Horda. El Cañón del Ventajo flanquea la arteria central que une Cerrotajo con Orgrimmar, abriendo caminos tanto hacia los riscos orientales como hacia los matorrales occidentales en dirección a la Granja Tor'kren. El cañón es el lugar de anidación de las arpías Dustwind, criaturas territoriales que atacan sin vacilar a los viajeros que se acercan demasiado a sus dormideros. Su presencia tan cerca de las rutas comerciales de la capital hace que limpiar estos barrancos sea una necesidad constante para los defensores de Durotar.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the Dustwind harpies from Razorwind Canyon is vital to keeping the main thoroughfare between Razor Hill and the capital of Orgrimmar safe for couriers and fresh recruits.",["race:Orc"]="The harpies nesting right along Durotar's central roadway are an insult to the security of the orcish homeland, requiring young warriors to cull their numbers."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Razorwind Canyon is located in central Durotar, flanking both sides of the main road running between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. Entrances lead into it north of Razor Hill, near Tor'kren Farm, and through a cave connecting to Drygulch Ravine.",["al"]={"razorwind canyon location","where is razorwind canyon","how to find razorwind canyon"},["q"]="Where is Razorwind Canyon located?"},{["a"]="The canyon is heavily inhabited by the Dustwind harpies. These aggressive, avian creatures nest in large clutches throughout the gullies and rocky outcroppings, preying on unwary travelers.",["al"]={"razorwind mobs","what lives in razorwind canyon","harpy canyon durotar"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit Razorwind Canyon?"},{["a"]="Razorwind Canyon borders the primary trade and travel route between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. The nesting harpies frequently harass couriers, supply caravans, and travelers passing along the central road.",["al"]={"why care about razorwind","orgrimmar threat razorwind"},["q"]="Why is the Horde concerned about this canyon?"},{["a"]="Yes. In addition to opening onto the main road, the canyon provides trails west toward Tor'kren Farm, as well as an eastern cavern leading into Drygulch Ravine.",["al"]={"canyon connections","where does razorwind lead"},["q"]="Does Razorwind Canyon connect to other areas?"}},["kw"]={"drygulch ravine","durotar","dustwind harpies","razor hill","razorwind canyon","tor'kren farm"},["n"]="Razorwind Canyon",["s"]="Razorwind Canyon is a winding, rocky gulch split across the main road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. Infested by the aggressive Dustwind harpies, the canyon poses a persistent danger to travelers moving north toward the Horde's capital.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Razorwind Canyon flanks the central artery linking Razor Hill to Orgrimmar, carving paths into both the eastern bluffs and the western scrublands toward Tor'kren Farm. The canyon is the nesting ground of the Dustwind harpies, territorial creatures that strike without hesitation at travelers who stray too close to their roosts. Their presence so near the capital's trade routes makes clearing out these gullies an ongoing necessity for the defenders of Durotar.",["t"]="A Threat on the High Road"},{["b"]="Beyond serving as harpy nests, the twists of Razorwind Canyon function as hidden routes through Durotar's red rock hills. The eastern branch tunnels deeply into the crags, providing a passage through a cavern into Drygulch Ravine. Because the harpies roost on the high perches and descend in flocks, unwary adventurers traversing these passes can easily find themselves surrounded and cut down.",["t"]="Passages and Ravines"}}}}}
t["subzone:red-rocks"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,293,35.621.0,24.440.0,33.290.0,36.229.0,27.224.0,35.216.0",["h"]="56dd04",["n"]="Roca Roja",["s"]="Roca Roja. Roca Roja es un imponente risco de arenisca en el noreste de Mulgore que sirve como cementerio ancestral sagrado para los tauren. Aquí, los campeones caídos son encomendados a la Madre Tierra mediante llamas purificadoras, y los jóvenes bravos viajan a sus tranquilas alturas para buscar la sabiduría de sus antepasados. Elevándose sobre las llanuras del noreste de Mulgore, las formaciones carmesíes de Roca Roja marcan un umbral sagrado entre el mundo de los vivos y el más allá. La tradición tauren reserva este solemne terreno para sus héroes más valerosos: caudillos, defensores y campeones que dieron sus vidas fundando y protegiendo Cima del Trueno. Sus restos son entregados al cielo y a la tierra a través de piras ceremoniales, devolviendo sus espíritus a la Madre Tierra y al Padre Cielo. Es igualmente un lugar de inicio espiritual, donde los jóvenes tauren completan sus ritos de iniciación honrando las tumbas ancestrales y comunicándose con el viento.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="The wind carries the sorrow of unsettled spirits disturbed by quilboar defilement, calling on shamanic rites to restore elemental balance and ancestral peace.",["race:Tauren"]="For your people, Red Rocks is sacred soil. The presence of foul quilboar rooting among your honored ancestors' pyres is an open outrage that demands cleansing."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Red Rocks serves as the premier ancestral burial ground and ceremonial rite site for the tauren of Mulgore. Fallen heroes and honored braves are cremated here to return their spirits to the Earth Mother, and young tauren visit its heights to honor the dead during their trials of adulthood.",["al"]={"why is red rocks important","red rocks purpose","what happens at red rocks"},["q"]="What is the purpose of Red Rocks?"},{["a"]="The Bristleback quilboar pushed out from their bramble burrows and overrun the plateau, defiling the burial mounds. Their intrusion is seen by the tauren as an intolerable sacrilege against the resting spirits of their ancestors.",["al"]={"quilboar at red rocks","who is invading red rocks","why are bristlebacks here"},["q"]="Why are there quilboar at Red Rocks?"},{["a"]="Burial at Red Rocks is an honor reserved for the most valiant tauren, including great warriors who fought alongside Cairne Bloodhoof to secure Mulgore and build Thunder Bluff, as well as heroes who died serving their tribes.",["al"]={"who is cremated here","red rocks dead","whose graves are these"},["q"]="Who is buried at Red Rocks?"},{["a"]="Beyond funerary pyres commended to the Earth Mother and Sky Father, the bluff is a focal point for the Rite of Wisdom, where tauren braves leave offerings and listen for the guidance of ancestral spirits on the wind.",["al"]={"rites at red rocks","tauren rituals red rocks"},["q"]="What ceremonies are performed here?"}},["kw"]={"bristleback","burial ground","earth mother","mulgore","quilboar","red rocks","rite of wisdom","thunder bluff"},["n"]="Red Rocks",["s"]="Red Rocks is a towering sandstone bluff in northeastern Mulgore that serves as a sacred ancestral burial ground for the tauren. Here, fallen champions are commended to the Earth Mother through cleansing flame, and young braves travel to its quiet heights to seek the wisdom of their forebears.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Rising high above the plains of northeastern Mulgore, the crimson formations of Red Rocks mark a sacred threshold between the living world and the next. Tauren tradition reserves this solemn ground for their most valiant heroes—chieftains, defenders, and champions who gave their lives founding and protecting Thunder Bluff. Their remains are surrendered to the sky and soil through ceremonial pyres, returning their spirits to the Earth Mother and Sky Father. It is equally a place of spiritual beginning, where young tauren complete their rites of passage by honoring the ancestral graves and communing with the wind.",["t"]="Hallowed Stones and Ancestral Pyres"},{["b"]="The enduring peace of Red Rocks has been shattered by the Bristleback quilboar. Creeping out from their dens, these aggressive scavengers have infested the sandstone ledges and desecrated the ancestral burial pyres with filth. This violation deeply affronts the spiritual traditions of Thunder Bluff. Shaman and lorekeepers now summon aid to cleanse the crags, driving out the Bristlebacks and reclaiming the sanctity of their resting dead.",["t"]="The Quilboar Desecration"}}}}}
t["subzone:remtravel-s-excavation"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,296,16.470.0,18.413.1,31.154.0,26.167.0,28.184.0,39.133.0",["h"]="87b77b",["n"]="Excavación de Tripirrem",["s"]="Excavación de Tripirrem. La Excavación de Tripirrem es un yacimiento arqueológico situado en los confines meridionales de Costa Oscura. Establecida por el prospector enano Tripirrem, la expedición topó recientemente con antiguas ruinas subterráneas, desenterrando inadvertidamente a hostiles troggs y gólems de piedra que no tardaron en invadir la cantera. El Prospector Tripirrem llegó a Costa Oscura en busca de reliquias de un pasado remoto, estableciendo una ambiciosa excavación lejos de la seguridad de Auberdine. Mientras excavaba estratos antiguos, su equipo desenterró un enjambre de troggs Gravelflint subterráneos junto a descomunales gólems de piedra sepultados bajo tierra. El lugar pasó al instante de ser una cantera académica a una zona de peligro, dispersando a los mineros y dejando a Tripirrem luchando por recuperar sus hallazgos más prometedores.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="Dwarven explorers of the Explorers' League are well known for seeking the secrets of the past, though unearthing dangerous troggs in foreign lands often leads to familiar headaches.",["race:NightElf"]="The kaldorei generally observe the deep meddling of Alliance dwarven picks with skepticism, especially when careless delving awakens wild troggs on Darkshore's ancient soil."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is an archaeological dig site in southern Darkshore founded by Prospector Remtravel, an explorer searching for ancient fossils and subterranean relics.",["al"]={"what is this place","darkshore dig site","remtravel site"},["q"]="What is Remtravel's Excavation?"},{["a"]="Dwarven miners dug too deeply into the earth and breached subterranean caverns, awakening a local tribe known as the Gravelflint troggs alongside dormant stone golems.",["al"]={"why troggs in darkshore","gravelflint troggs","where did troggs come from"},["q"]="Why are there troggs here?"},{["a"]="He is a dwarven archaeologist leading the excavation. Known for his keen eye for artifacts as well as his absent-minded nature, he lost track of a key fossil when his dig was attacked.",["al"]={"who is remtravel","prospector remtravel lore"},["q"]="Who is Prospector Remtravel?"},{["a"]="Remtravel discovered an unusual fossil imbued with strange, mystic properties shortly before the troggs surged from the lower depths.",["al"]={"what did they find","remtravel fossil","mystic fossil"},["q"]="What kind of relic was discovered here?"}},["kw"]={"darkshore","excavation","fossil","golem","gravelflint","prospector","remtravel","trogg"},["n"]="Remtravel's Excavation",["s"]="Remtravel's Excavation is an archaeological dig site located in the southern reaches of Darkshore. Established by the dwarven Prospector Remtravel, the expedition recently struck ancient subterranean ruins, inadvertently unearthing hostile troggs and stone golems that quickly overran the quarry.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Prospector Remtravel came to Darkshore in search of relics of the distant past, establishing an ambitious dig far from the safety of Auberdine. While excavating ancient strata, his team unearthed a swarm of subterranean Gravelflint troggs alongside hulking stone golems buried beneath the earth. The site was instantly transformed from a scholarly quarry into a hazard zone, scattering the miners and leaving Remtravel scrambling to retrieve his most promising findings.",["t"]="A Quarry Overrun"},{["b"]="Before the excavation descended into chaos, Remtravel had uncovered a rare fossil radiating curious mystic properties. In the panic of the trogg onslaught—and hindered by his notorious absent-mindedness—the prospector misplaced the valuable relic amid the sprawling dirt pits. Venturing down into the dig to recover it means braving both the vicious troggs and the ancient automatons awakened by the pickaxes.",["t"]="The Missing Fossil"}}}}}
t["subzone:render-s-rock"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,300,34.483.0,24.411.1,31.144.0,27.164.0,34.166.0,50.220.0",["h"]="7e65a4",["n"]="Roca de Render",["s"]="Roca de Render. Roca de Render es una caverna fortificada oculta en los riscos noroccidentales de las Montañas Crestagrana, situada cerca del paso elevado que conduce hacia Las Estepas Ardientes. Controlada por los feroces orcos Roca Negra, sirve como reducto avanzado y punto de partida activo para sus incursiones en los valles de abajo. Escavada en las escarpadas alturas al norte de Villa del Lago, Roca de Render sirve como un sistema de cuevas fortificado para el invasor Clan Roca Negra. Desde este reducto defendible cerca del paso de montaña hacia Las Estepas Ardientes, veteranos orcos Roca Negra orquestan ataques contra los defensores locales de Crestagrana. Sus profundidades sombrías están estrictamente vigiladas, lo que convierte cualquier incursión en su interior en una empresa peligrosa para aquellos que buscan interrumpir las líneas de suministro orcas o rescatar a los cautivos perdidos en el conflicto en curso.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance fighters, Render's Rock represents one of the most entrenched Blackrock positions in Redridge, and clearing it is vital for freeing Corporal Keeshan and protecting Lakeshire."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Render's Rock is situated in the far northwestern peaks of the Redridge Mountains, nestled near the path leading north into the Burning Steppes.",["al"]={"renders rock location","where is renders rock","find renders rock"},["q"]="Where is Render's Rock located?"},{["a"]="The cave is occupied by formidable Blackrock orcs who use the crag as a redoubt to coordinate attacks and oversee the mountain passes bordering the Burning Steppes.",["al"]={"who lives in renders rock","renders rock enemies","who holds renders rock"},["q"]="Who controls Render's Rock?"},{["a"]="Corporal Keeshan, a wounded veteran soldier of the Alliance garrison, is held captive inside Render's Rock and requires assistance to safely escape back to Lakeshire.",["al"]={"keeshan location","captive in renders rock","who is trapped in renders rock"},["q"]="Who is imprisoned inside the cave?"},{["a"]="Because it harbors experienced Blackrock warriors right above the Redridge valley, Render's Rock poses an immediate threat to the town of Lakeshire and allows the orcs to maintain a foothold south of the Burning Steppes.",["al"]={"why attack renders rock","renders rock threat","importance of renders rock"},["q"]="Why is this cave important to Lakeshire's defense?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock orcs","burning steppes","corporal keeshan","keeshan","redridge","render's rock","renders rock"},["n"]="Render's Rock",["s"]="Render's Rock is a cavern stronghold tucked into the northwestern crags of the Redridge Mountains, sitting near the high pass leading toward the Burning Steppes. Controlled by the fierce Blackrock orcs, it serves as a forward redoubt and an active staging ground for their raids on the valleys below.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved into the rugged heights north of Lakeshire, Render's Rock serves as a fortified cave system for the invading Blackrock clan. From this defensible redoubt near the mountain pass to the Burning Steppes, veteran Blackrock orcs orchestrate attacks against the local defenders of Redridge. Its shadowed depths are strictly guarded, making any foray inside a perilous undertaking for those seeking to disrupt the orcish supply lines or recover captives lost in the ongoing conflict.",["t"]="A Blackrock Bastion in the Heights"},{["b"]="Beyond its strategic value to the orcs, Render's Rock holds grim importance for the defenders of Lakeshire. The wounded Redridge soldier Corporal Keeshan is held captive within its recesses. Deep behind enemy lines and isolated from his companions, Keeshan's captivity represents both the audacity of the Blackrock incursions and the high price the local garrison has paid trying to keep the mountain road open.",["t"]="A Hostage in the Shadows"}}}}}
t["subzone:render-s-valley"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,279,27.484.0,25.498.0,29.186.0,57.188.0,37.197.0,45.187.0",["h"]="52d6de",["n"]="Valle de Render",["s"]="Valle de Render. El Valle de Render es un campamento escondido y controlado por orcos Rocanegra en el sureste de las Montañas Crestagrana. Mucho menos atrincherado que las enormes fortalezas de Petravista, supone no obstante una amenaza constante para los viajeros cercanos y alberga cautivos apresados en las tierras circundantes. Escondido entre las crestas rocosas al sureste del Lago Sempiterno, el Valle de Render sirve como campamento auxiliar para los orcos Rocanegra que operan en Crestagrana. A diferencia de las fortalezas fuertemente fortificadas y las torres de piedra de los riscos del norte, el valle consta de una modesta agrupación de tiendas de guerra, estandartes y puestos de vigilancia. A pesar de ser más pequeño y estar menos armado que las fuerzas principales del clan, los guerreros de aquí asaltan los caminos locales, hostigan a los viajeros y mantienen prisioneros capturados bajo vigilancia en toscas jaulas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The camp is a secondary Blackrock raiding outpost that threatens southern Redridge, making its clearing vital for securing trade and travel in Lakeshire.",["profession:Tailoring"]="The Captured Servant of Azora imprisoned in the orc camp offers unique tailoring patterns and materials to craftsmen willing to fight through the sentries to reach him."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The valley is occupied by the Blackrock clan, an aggressive orcish faction that has pushed south from the Burning Steppes into Redridge to conquer territory and harass human settlements.",["al"]={"who is in renders valley","renders valley orcs","what clan is in renders valley"},["q"]="Who controls Render's Valley?"},{["a"]="No. The Blackrock warriors stationed in Render's Valley are generally younger or less formidable skirmishers compared to the hardened elite forces garrisoning Stonewatch Keep to the north.",["al"]={"renders valley difficulty","how strong are the orcs here"},["q"]="Are the orcs here as dangerous as the ones at Stonewatch?"},{["a"]="A servant affiliated with the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest was captured by the Blackrock clan and held here in a cage. Those brave enough to reach him can acquire specialized tailoring supplies.",["al"]={"renders valley captive","servant of azora redridge","renders valley tailor"},["q"]="Who is the prisoner kept in the camp?"},{["a"]="Yes. A steep, unofficial mountain trail winds through the southern bluffs just past Render's Valley, offering a hidden shortcut directly into the northern marches of the Swamp of Sorrows.",["al"]={"path to swamp of sorrows","renders valley mountain pass","redridge to swamp shortcut"},["q"]="Can you reach the Swamp of Sorrows from here?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock orcs","redridge","render's valley","renders valley","servant of azora","swamp of sorrows pass"},["n"]="Render's Valley",["s"]="Render's Valley is a tucked-away encampment held by Blackrock orcs in the southeastern Redridge Mountains. Far less entrenched than the massive fortresses of Stonewatch, it nonetheless poses a persistent threat to nearby travelers and hosts captives taken from surrounding lands.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked among the rocky ridges southeast of Lake Everstill, Render's Valley serves as an auxiliary camp for the Blackrock orcs operating in Redridge. Unlike the heavily fortified keeps and stone towers of the northern cliffs, the valley consists of a modest cluster of war tents, banners, and sentry outposts. Despite being smaller and less armed than the clan's core forces, the warriors here raid local roads, harass travelers, and keep captured prisoners in crude cages under guard.",["t"]="A Foothold in the Southeast"},{["b"]="Beyond the war parties roaming its dirt paths, the valley holds unexpected points of interest for intrepid scouts. Human prisoners have occasionally been sighted within the camp, including a captive servant connected to the Tower of Azora who managed to trade specialist goods right under his captors' noses. Additionally, rugged and unmarked pathways through the high southern bluffs behind the valley allow daring pathfinders to slip across the border into the murky bogs of the Swamp of Sorrows.",["t"]="Secret Paths and Captives"}}}}}
t["subzone:ridgepoint-tower"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,309,30.471.0,24.421.0,25.209.0,32.143.0,45.206.0,34.155.0",["h"]="ed30b2",["n"]="Torre de la Peña",["s"]="Torre de la Peña. La Torre de la Peña es un puesto de guardia fortificado que vigila la frontera oriental del Bosque de Elwynn. Guarnecida por la Guardia de Ventormenta, sirve como baluarte de alerta temprana contra las incursiones hostiles que amenazan el corazón del reino. Sus guardias vigilan constantemente los peligrosos pasos que conducen a las tierras salvajes vecinas. Erigida como centinela en el terreno elevado del este del Bosque de Elwynn, la Torre de la Peña marca el último bastión de la autoridad directa de Ventormenta antes de que se impongan las tierras salvajes indómitas. La guarnición apostada aquí mantiene una vigilancia constante sobre los valles y caminos circundantes. Con las crecientes tensiones en todo el continente, esta atalaya de piedra garantiza que las amenazas invasoras sean detectadas y contenidas antes de que puedan poner en peligro las granjas y asentamientos más cercanos a Northshire y Villadorada.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Soldiers and mercenaries alike can respect the stoic resolve of the guardsmen holding such an exposed border outpost against surrounding hostiles.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, Ridgepoint Tower is a reassuring beacon of safety and order before crossing into the perilous passes of Redridge or the haunted roads of Duskwood."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Ridgepoint Tower is a fortified scout tower operated by the Stormwind Guard in eastern Elwynn Forest. It serves as a frontline watchpost tasked with alerting and protecting the kingdom from hostile intrusions.",["al"]={"ridgepoint tower elwynn","what is this guard tower","east elwynn tower"},["q"]="What is Ridgepoint Tower?"},{["a"]="The tower is held and garrisoned by guardsmen and scouts loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind, operating under the command of the Stormwind Guard.",["al"]={"who is at ridgepoint tower","who owns ridgepoint tower"},["q"]="Who controls and mans the tower?"},{["a"]="The guards watch for gnolls and invading orcs spilling out of the Redridge Mountains, undead crossing from the blighted groves of Duskwood, and Defias bandits operating in clandestine woodland camps nearby.",["al"]={"enemies near ridgepoint","what is attacking ridgepoint","why is the tower here"},["q"]="What threats does the garrison watch out for?"},{["a"]="It stands on the elevated ground in the far eastern reaches of Elwynn Forest, near the borders connecting Elwynn with both Redridge Mountains and Duskwood.",["al"]={"ridgepoint tower location","where is ridgepoint"},["q"]="Where is Ridgepoint Tower located?"}},["kw"]={"defias","duskwood","elwynn forest","gnolls","redridge","ridgepoint tower","stormwind guard","watchtower"},["n"]="Ridgepoint Tower",["s"]="Ridgepoint Tower is a fortified guard post watching the eastern frontier of Elwynn Forest. Manned by the Stormwind Guard, it serves as an early warning bulwark against hostile incursions threatening the heart of the kingdom. Its guards keep vigil over the perilous corridors leading to neighboring wilderness.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing sentinel on the high ground of eastern Elwynn Forest, Ridgepoint Tower marks the final bastion of direct Stormwind authority before the untamed wilds take over. The garrison stationed here keeps a constant watch over the surrounding valleys and roads. With tensions mounting across the continent, this stone watchtower ensures that encroaching threats are spotted and checked before they can endanger the farms and settlements closer to Northshire and Goldshire.",["t"]="Sentinel of the Eastern Border"},{["b"]="Ridgepoint Tower faces pressure from multiple frontiers at once. To the east lie the Redridge Mountains, home to aggressive gnoll packs and blackrock orc raiders who test human defenses. Across the southern river looms the shadowy timberline of Duskwood, with its prowling undead horrors. Closer to home, rogue Defias Brotherhood bandits prowl the wilderness camps, eager to exploit any gap in the guard's defensive line.",["t"]="Threats on Every Horizon"}}}}}
t["subzone:rocktusk-farm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,241,26.449.0,31.159.0,31.140.0,34.187.0",["h"]="1eb61d",["n"]="Granja Rocamuela",["s"]="Granja Rocamuela. La Granja Rocamuela es un pequeño rancho de cerdos situado en el norte de Durotar, siguiendo el camino a las puertas de Orgrimmar. Resguardada cerca de los accesos fortificados de la capital, la granja suministra carne y provisiones vitales a los habitantes de la ciudad. Excavada en el árido suelo de Durotar, la Granja Rocamuela se dedica a la cría de cerdos resistentes y adaptados al duro clima desértico. Debido al terreno notoriamente seco y pedregoso de Durotar, cultivar resulta difícil, lo que convierte a las granjas de cerdos domésticos en un sustento esencial para alimentar a la creciente población de Orgrimmar. Situada cerca del perímetro fortificado de la capital, la hacienda goza de un grado de seguridad rara vez visto en las inhóspitas tierras salvajes de los cañones rojos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Settled just outside the capital, the swine reared here are critical sustenance for the warriors and laborers stationed in Orgrimmar.",["profession:Cooking"]="The pigs raised on the farm are prized by Horde cooks searching for fresh pork, ribs, and savory cuts to roast."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Rocktusk Farm is a domestic pig farm. It raises swine to supply fresh meat and provisions to the neighboring capital of Orgrimmar, where arable land is scarce.",["al"]={"what is this place","rocktusk farm purpose","why are there pigs here"},["q"]="What is Rocktusk Farm used for?"},{["a"]="The farm sits in northern Durotar, located just southwest down the road from the main gates of Orgrimmar and nestled along the rocky bluffs.",["al"]={"where is rocktusk farm","rocktusk farm location"},["q"]="Where is Rocktusk Farm located?"},{["a"]="Its close proximity to Orgrimmar and nearby Horde military patrols keeps it safer than most outlying homesteads in Durotar, though wild beasts and roaming pests still prowl the outskirts.",["al"]={"is rocktusk farm safe","dangers at rocktusk farm"},["q"]="Is the farm safe from wild beasts?"}},["kw"]={"durotar","horde provisions","orgrimmar","pig farm","rocktusk farm","swine"},["n"]="Rocktusk Farm",["s"]="Rocktusk Farm is a small swine ranch situated in northern Durotar just down the road outside the gates of Orgrimmar. Tucked near the fortified approaches of the capital, the stead supplies vital meat and provisions to the city's inhabitants.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved out of the arid soil of Durotar, Rocktusk Farm is dedicated to raising hardy swine suited to the rough desert climate. Due to Durotar's notoriously dry and stony ground, raising crops is difficult, making domestic swine farms an essential lifeline for feeding Orgrimmar's burgeoning population. Nestled close to the capital's fortified perimeter, the homestead enjoys a degree of safety rarely found in the harsh wilds of the red canyonlands.",["t"]="Provisions for the Capital"}}}}}
t["subzone:rogues-quarter"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,226,24.540.0,18.454.0,37.114.0,32.181.0,61.226.0",["h"]="8ea698",["n"]="Barrio de los Pícaros",["s"]="Barrio de los Pícaros. Barrio de los Pícaros es un distrito tenuemente iluminado en el ala sureste de Entrañas. Sirve como centro de operaciones para los exploradores, asesinos y operativos del submundo de los Renegados, junto con los artesanos que los respaldan. Escondido en el cuadrante sureste de la ciudad subterránea, Barrio de los Pícaros reúne a los supervivientes más astutos y letales de los Renegados. En vida, muchos fueron ladrones, carteristas o filos silenciosos al servicio del Reino de Lordaeron; en la muerte, su pericia en el sigilo, los venenos y el despiste se ha reorientado para proteger a la naciente nación de la Plaga y de La Cruzada Escarlata. El distrito bulle con una discreta actividad, ofreciendo un refugio clandestino donde los operativos afilan sus dagas, elaboran toxinas mortíferas y perfeccionan habilidades encubiertas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="For Forsaken and Horde assassins, this quarter is the premier hub for mastering stealth, learning combat techniques, and stocking up on lethal poison reagents.",["profession:Engineering"]="Tinkers visit the Rogues' Quarter to learn schematics and craft bombs, gadgets, and mechanical tools favored by undercover agents."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Rogues' Quarter is situated in the southeastern section of the Undercity's outer ring, past the Trade Quarter.",["al"]={"rogues quarter location","where is rogues quarter","undercity rogues quarter map"},["q"]="Where is the Rogues' Quarter located?"},{["a"]="The quarter houses trainers for rogues, as well as instructors for leatherworking, skinning, engineering, and first aid. Poison vendors are also stationed nearby to supply reagents.",["al"]={"rogues quarter trainers","undercity rogue trainer","who trains in rogues quarter"},["q"]="What trainers can be found here?"},{["a"]="Surrounded by hostile forces like the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade, the Forsaken rely heavily on espionage, assassination, and hit-and-run tactics to defend their territory, making covert operatives vital to their survival.",["al"]={"why do forsaken need rogues","forsaken assassins","undercity rogue lore"},["q"]="Why do the Forsaken maintain a dedicated district for rogues?"}},["kw"]={"engineering","forsaken","leatherworking","poison vendor","rogue trainer","rogues quarter","rogues' quarter","skinning","undercity"},["n"]="Rogues' Quarter",["s"]="The Rogues' Quarter is a dimly lit district in the southeastern wing of the Undercity. It serves as the staging ground for the Forsaken's scouts, assassins, and underworld operatives, along with the craftsmen who support them.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the southeastern quadrant of the subterranean city, the Rogues' Quarter gathers the Forsaken's most cunning and lethal survivors. In life, many were thieves, cutpurses, or silent blades for the Kingdom of Lordaeron; in death, their expertise in stealth, poisons, and misdirection has been repurposed to protect the fledgling nation from the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade. The district hums with quiet activity, offering a covert haven where operatives sharpen their daggers, brew deadly toxins, and hone clandestine skills.",["t"]="Shadows of the Undercity"},{["b"]="Beyond stealth and assassination, the Rogues' Quarter is home to the specialized trades that enable undercover survival. Artisans gather here to instruct travelers in leatherworking and skinning, turning raw hides into light, silent armor. The clatter of engineering benches echoes through the stone halls as tinkers assemble gadgets, while field medics and apothecaries provide instruction in first aid and vend lethal poisons essential for covert work.",["t"]="Tools of the Trade"}}}}}
t["subzone:rolling-plains"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,296,25.493.0,19.418.0,48.256.0,53.268.0,49.179.0,42.122.0",["h"]="1c926f",["n"]="Las Llanuras Onduladas",["s"]="Las Llanuras Onduladas. Las Llanuras Onduladas abarcan la extensión meridional de Mulgore, extendiéndose entre Poblado Pezuña de Sangre y la frontera con Los Baldíos. Estos pastizales azotados por el viento albergan prósperas manadas de fauna salvaje, pero también son un punto de constante vigilancia debido a los centauros asaltantes que merodean y a las agresivas arpías. Extendiéndose hacia el sur desde Poblado Pezuña de Sangre hacia las puertas naturales de tierra que conducen a Los Baldíos, Las Llanuras Onduladas personifican las vastas y abiertas praderas del hogar tauren. La zona rebosa de piezas de caza esenciales para las tribus, como lobos de las praderas, manadas de kodos, pumas de las llanuras y veloces zancudos. Para los jóvenes cazadores que demuestran su valía ante los ancianos, estas amplias sabanas sirven como un campo de pruebas indispensable donde el rastreo, la paciencia y la reverencia por la naturaleza se ponen a prueba.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="With ample herds of kodo, tallstriders, wolves, and cougars, the Rolling Plains offer an ideal wilderness for honing tracking skills, gathering provisions, and taming first animal companions.",["race:Tauren"]="The Rolling Plains provide vital hunting grounds for the newly unified tribes, but the intrusion of ancient centaur enemies so close to Bloodhoof Village makes guarding this southern corridor a matter of tribal survival."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The grasslands support a rich variety of native fauna, including roaming herds of wild kodo, nimble tallstriders, prowling prairie wolves, and stalking flatland cougars. These beasts provide vital meat, hides, and sinew for the tribes of Bloodhoof Village.",["al"]={"rolling plains wildlife","mobs rolling plains","animals mulgore plains"},["q"]="What animals can be found on the Rolling Plains?"},{["a"]="The Rolling Plains border the eastern passes into the Barrens, making them the only region in Mulgore where centaur raiders have managed to breach the perimeter. Marauding outriders constantly scout the plains, probing tauren defenses and threatening isolated hunters.",["al"]={"centaur in mulgore","why centaur rolling plains","centaur outriders"},["q"]="Why are centaur found wandering this part of Mulgore?"},{["a"]="Aside from roaming centaur scouts, a dangerous enclave of Windfury harpies nests along the eastern crags of the region, preying upon unwary travelers and harassing local wildlife.",["al"]={"harpies rolling plains","dangers rolling plains"},["q"]="What other hostile creatures threaten the plains?"},{["a"]="The plains cover much of southern Mulgore, stretching from Bloodhoof Village to the mountain border adjoining the Barrens.",["al"]={"rolling plains location","where are rolling plains","boundaries rolling plains"},["q"]="Where do the Rolling Plains begin and end?"}},["kw"]={"bloodhoof village","centaur","harpies","kodo","mulgore","rolling plains","tallstrider","windfury"},["n"]="Rolling Plains",["s"]="The Rolling Plains span the southern expanse of Mulgore, stretching between Bloodhoof Village and the border of the Barrens. These windswept grasslands are home to thriving herds of wildlife, but they are also a point of perpetual vigilance due to prowling centaur raiders and aggressive harpies.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spanning south from Bloodhoof Village toward the natural earthen gates leading into the Barrens, the Rolling Plains embody the vast open ranges of the tauren homeland. The area teems with wild game essential to the tribes, including prairie wolves, kodo herds, flatland cougars, and swift tallstriders. For young hunters proving their worth to the elders, these sweeping savannahs serve as an indispensable proving ground where tracking, patience, and reverence for nature are put to the test.",["t"]="Heart of Southern Mulgore"},{["b"]="Despite Mulgore's naturally fortified ring of bluffs, the Rolling Plains remain uniquely exposed to outside threats. It is the only frontier where aggressive centaur outriders have managed to push past defensive perimeters to harass passing travelers and hunting parties. Adding to the peril, a nest of predatory Windfury harpies roosts in the eastern crags, swooping down upon stray game and vulnerable nomadic camps.",["t"]="Encroaching Dangers"}}}}}
t["subzone:rotting-orchard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,253,20.573.0,42.231.0,49.197.0,37.172.0,42.223.0",["h"]="de9c0e",["n"]="El Vergel Pútrido",["s"]="El Vergel Pútrido. El Vergel Pútrido es una plantación de frutales marchita y abandonada situada en el sur de Bosque del Ocaso. En su día fue una fuente de cosechas para el cercano asentamiento de Villa Oscura, pero ha caído en la ruina y ahora está infestada por rapaces depredadores lupinos conocidos como la manada de los Nocturnos. Ubicado al este de la ruinosa Hacienda Yorgen y al oeste del Cementerio del Jardín Sereno, el Vergel Pútrido se erige como un lúgubre testimonio del declive de Bosque del Ocaso. Los árboles se doblan por el peso de frutos marchitos y podridos, mientras que graneros y dependencias ruinosas han sido convertidos en toscos campamentos por los huargen Nocturnos. Los acechadores nocturnos merodean entre la maleza retorcida, mientras que lanzadores de conjuros oscuros conocidos como tejesombras tejen su siniestra magia entre la madera en descomposición. La manada responde ante su feroz líder, Marus, que acecha por los bosques circundantes vigilando su dominio robado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The twisted trees and ruined outbuildings provide prime stalking ground, but the predatory senses and spellcraft of the Nightbane pack make it an ambush waiting to happen.",["faction:Alliance"]="The encroachment of the Nightbane worgen at the Rotting Orchard poses a direct predatory threat to the fragile security of Darkshire just up the road."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The orchard is completely infested by the Nightbane pack, a faction of ravenous worgen. These include cunning prowlers called Nightbane Stalkers, dark spellcasters known as Nightbane Shadow Weavers, and their roaming leader, Marus.",["al"]={"rotting orchard mobs","who lives in rotting orchard","what is at rotting orchard"},["q"]="What creatures occupy the Rotting Orchard?"},{["a"]="The Rotting Orchard lies in southern Duskwood, southwest of the town of Darkshire. It is nestled right between the ruined Yorgen Farmstead to its west and the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery to its east.",["al"]={"rotting orchard location","where is rotting orchard","how to find rotting orchard"},["q"]="Where is the Rotting Orchard located in Duskwood?"},{["a"]="The packleader of the worgen here is named Marus. He prowls the territory between the decaying orchard grounds and his nearby den, aggressively defending the pack's domain.",["al"]={"rotting orchard boss","packleader marus","who leads nightbane"},["q"]="Who leads the worgen in this orchard?"},{["a"]="No. Like many surrounding homesteads in Duskwood, it was once a productive farm and fruit grove supporting the local human populace before dark curses and supernatural horrors overtook the region and drove the farmers away.",["al"]={"orchard history","why is orchard rotting"},["q"]="Was this place always overrun by monsters?"}},["kw"]={"darkshire","duskwood","marus","nightbane","rotting orchard","shadow weavers","worgen"},["n"]="Rotting Orchard",["s"]="The Rotting Orchard is a blighted, abandoned fruit grove situated in southern Duskwood. Once a source of harvest for the nearby settlement of Darkshire, it has fallen into ruin and is now overrun by ravenous lupine predators known as the Nightbane pack.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located east of the ruined Yorgen Farmstead and west of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery, the Rotting Orchard stands as a grim testament to Duskwood's decline. The trees hang heavy with withered, spoiled fruit, while dilapidated barns and outbuildings have been converted into rough encampments by the Nightbane worgen. Nightbane Stalkers prowl the twisted brush, while dark casters known as Shadow Weavers weave their sinister magic amid the decaying timber. The pack answers to their fierce leader, Marus, who prowls the surrounding woods keeping watch over their stolen domain.",["t"]="Den of the Nightbane"}}}}}
t["subzone:royal-gallery"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,249,16.443.0,35.155.0,47.187.0,38.105.0,71.221.0",["h"]="293c29",["n"]="Galería Real",["s"]="Galería Real. Escondida en el interior del Castillo de Ventormenta tras el jardín del patio, la Galería Real sirve como una tranquila sala del recuerdo. Exhibe magníficas estatuas y bellas obras de arte en honor a figuras destacadas de la historia del reino y de la Gran Alianza. La Galería Real se encuentra adyacente a la Biblioteca Real, justo más allá del verde jardín interior del Castillo de Ventormenta. La sala alberga estatuas de imponentes figuras que forjaron el reino: el Rey Llane Wrynn, el soberano caído de Ventormenta; el Gran Almirante Daelin Valiente de Kul Tiras; y Mara Fordragón, antepasada del actual regente. Sirve a la vez como museo privado de la nobleza y como un retiro tranquilo para visitantes cortesanos como Lady Dena Kennedy.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The gallery stands as a quiet monument to the sacrifices of the Alliance, paying homage to legendary leaders like Daelin Proudmoore and King Llane.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, this hall honors the legacy of House Wrynn and House Fordragon, preserving their royal heritage within the keep."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Royal Gallery is located inside Stormwind Keep. Head through the keep past the small interior courtyard park, situated right next to the Royal Library.",["al"]={"royal gallery location","how to get to royal gallery","where is it"},["q"]="Where is the Royal Gallery located?"},{["a"]="The gallery features grand statues honoring King Llane Wrynn, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, and Mara Fordragon, celebrating the lineage and valor of the kingdom and its closest allies.",["al"]={"statues in royal gallery","who are the statues of","who is honored here"},["q"]="Which historical figures are commemorated here?"},{["a"]="Lady Dena Kennedy can frequently be found admiring the fine art and reflective atmosphere of the gallery.",["al"]={"who is here","npcs in royal gallery","lady dena kennedy"},["q"]="Who can be found visiting the gallery?"},{["a"]="While situated immediately next to one another in the royal wing of Stormwind Keep, they are distinct chambers. The library houses royal archives and scholars, while the gallery focuses on fine art and memorial sculpture.",["al"]={"royal gallery vs library","is it part of the library"},["q"]="What is the difference between the Royal Gallery and the Royal Library?"}},["kw"]={"daelin proudmoore","dena kennedy","llane wrynn","mara fordragon","royal gallery","statues","stormwind keep"},["n"]="Royal Gallery",["s"]="Tucked away inside Stormwind Keep past the courtyard garden, the Royal Gallery serves as a quiet hall of remembrance. It displays magnificent statues and fine works of art honoring prominent figures from the kingdom's history and the Grand Alliance.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The Royal Gallery sits adjacent to the Royal Library, just beyond the verdant interior garden of Stormwind Keep. The hall houses statues of towering figures who shaped the realm: King Llane Wrynn, the fallen ruler of Stormwind; Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras; and Mara Fordragon, ancestor of the current Regent. It serves as both a private museum of noble heritage and a quiet retreat for courtly visitors like Lady Dena Kennedy.",["t"]="A Hall of Heroes"}}}}}
t["subzone:royal-library"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,302,25.545.0,25.242.0,35.204.0,21.167.0,37.222.0,37.272.0",["h"]="1f2547",["n"]="Biblioteca Real",["s"]="Biblioteca Real. Escondida en lo profundo del ala de piedra del Castillo de Ventormenta, la Biblioteca Real preserva la memoria colectiva, los pergaminos de crónicas y los tratados del reino. Bajo la atenta mirada del bibliotecario jefe Milton Gavilla, sus estantes albergan registros cruciales de guerras antiguas, leyendas perdidas y los reinos de más allá del mar. Mientras Castillo de Ventormenta rebosa de guardias con armadura e intrigas cortesanas, su Biblioteca Real ofrece un remanso de tranquilidad erudita. Supervisada por Milton Gavilla, la sala sirve como el principal archivo de la historia de los humanos del sur, conservando textos supervivientes de antes de la Primera Guerra junto con crónicas militares recientes y tomos recuperados. Los eruditos, sacerdotes y viajeros de la Alianza son libres de consultar sus tratados abiertos, que abarcan desde la formación de la original Alianza de Lordaeron hasta el reciente surgimiento de la Horda de Thrall en Kalimdor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="For scholars of the arcane, the library offers rare primary sources on Tirisfal's past, ancient dragon hunts, and the legacy of the Last Guardian.",["faction:Alliance"]="The shelves preserve the foundational treaties and war chronicles that bind the human, dwarven, and elven peoples across generations of conflict."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is located inside Stormwind Keep, the royal fortress resting in the eastern sector of Stormwind City. Once through the keep's grand foyer, take the corridors leading into the scholar and archive wings.",["al"]={"where is the library","stormwind library location","how to find library"},["q"]="Where is the Royal Library located?"},{["a"]="Milton Sheaf serves as the head librarian. He manages the archive's records and assists scholars and adventurers seeking missing volumes or specific kingdom treatises.",["al"]={"who is the librarian","head librarian","milton sheaf"},["q"]="Who runs the library?"},{["a"]="Visitors can read historical works covering the Alliance of Lordaeron, the Guardians of Tirisfal, the aftermath of the Second War, and reports regarding the New Horde, alongside regional histories of Stormwind and Alterac.",["al"]={"books in library","readable lore books","what to read"},["q"]="What kinds of books can be read here?"},{["a"]="After the defeat of the Horde in the Second War, the dangerous spellbook was secured within the Royal Library for safekeeping. However, Alterac conspirators stole it, crossing paths with Teron Gorefiend's death knights who were staging an assault to claim it for Ner'zhul.",["al"]={"book of medivh stormwind","medivh book stolen"},["q"]="Why was the Book of Medivh kept here?"}},["kw"]={"book of medivh","mathias shaw","milton sheaf","royal library","stormwind keep","stormwind library"},["n"]="Royal Library",["s"]="Tucked deep within the stone wing of Stormwind Keep, the Royal Library preserves the collective memory, chronicle scrolls, and treatises of the kingdom. Under the watchful eye of Head Librarian Milton Sheaf, its shelves hold crucial records of ancient wars, lost legends, and the realms beyond the sea.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While Stormwind Keep bristles with armored guards and courtly intrigue, its Royal Library offers an island of scholarly quiet. Overseen by Milton Sheaf, the hall serves as the premier archive of southern human history, preserving surviving texts from before the First War alongside recent military chronicles and recovered tomes. Alliance scholars, priests, and travelers are free to browse its open treatises, which cover everything from the formation of the original Alliance of Lordaeron to the recent emergence of Thrall's Horde in Kalimdor.",["t"]="A Repository of the Realm"},{["b"]="The library has not always remained unmolested by outside conflicts. Following the Second War, the dangerous Book of Medivh was stored within its vaults, drawing Alterac infiltrators and death knights sent by Ner'zhul in a brazen castle raid.",["t"]="Shadows Among the Shelves"}}}}}
t["subzone:ruins-of-mathystra"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,285,24.507.0,38.584.0,38.249.0,46.209.0,22.242.0,43.247.0",["h"]="31e863",["n"]="Ruinas de Mathystra",["s"]="Ruinas de Mathystra. Las Ruinas de Mathystra son los restos derruidos de una antigua ciudad de los elfos de la noche situada a lo largo de la costa norte de Costa Oscura. Destrozadas durante el Gran Cataclismo hace diez mil años, las ruinas costeras están ahora infestadas por hostiles naga Stormscale y merodeadas por escurridizos Ghost Sabers. Hace diez milenios, Mathystra era un bullicioso asentamiento de los elfos de la noche, hogar de nobles Altonato de alto rango. Cuando el Pozo de la Eternidad colapsó durante el Gran Cataclismo, olas cataclísmicas destrozaron la ciudad costera, derribando sus grandes arcos de mármol y arrastrando gran parte de su sillería al mar. Los elfos de la noche supervivientes abandonaron la ciudad en ruinas en favor de aldeas boscosas más pequeñas más al sur, dejando los patios hundidos y los cimientos agrietados de Mathystra a merced de los implacables elementos costeros.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The translucent Ghost Sabers prowling among the rubble of Mathystra are renowned beasts for beastmasters seeking a striking companion with ties to the spirit world.",["race:NightElf"]="Mathystra stands as a somber monument to the hubris of the ancient Highborne, whose reckless sorcery brought cataclysm down upon their own grand coastal settlements."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Mathystra was a thriving night elven city built during the height of the ancient Highborne empire. It was shattered and largely drowned ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering, when the Well of Eternity exploded and cleaved Kalimdor apart.",["al"]={"mathystra history","who built mathystra","what was mathystra"},["q"]="What used to be here before the ruins?"},{["a"]="The ruins are currently occupied by the Stormscale naga, who have emerged from the sea to claim the sunken pavilions and coastlines. They aggressively attack any land-dwellers who intrude upon their territory.",["al"]={"who lives in mathystra","mathystra mobs","who is at mathystra"},["q"]="Who controls the Ruins of Mathystra right now?"},{["a"]="Ghost Sabers are ethereal, translucent felines that haunt the ruined stonework of Mathystra. Hunters often seek them out along the coast, though disturbing the ancient figurines in the area is known to draw these spirits out from the shadows.",["al"]={"ghost saber mathystra","glowing cat darkshore","ghost sabers"},["q"]="What are Ghost Sabers?"},{["a"]="Young night elves and scholars occasionally venture into the ruins to recover ancient Highborne relics left behind after the Sundering. However, the presence of fierce Stormscale naga makes recovering these historical treasures extremely perilous.",["al"]={"mathystra relics","why go to mathystra"},["q"]="Why do night elves visit these ruins today?"}},["kw"]={"darkshore","ghost saber","great sundering","highborne","mathystra","naga","ruins of mathystra","stormscale"},["n"]="Ruins of Mathystra",["s"]="The Ruins of Mathystra are the crumbled remnants of an ancient night elven city sitting along the northern coast of Darkshore. Shattered during the Great Sundering ten thousand years ago, the coastal ruins are now overrun by hostile Stormscale naga and prowled by elusive Ghost Sabers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Ten millennia ago, Mathystra stood as a bustling night elven settlement, home to high-ranking Highborne nobility. When the Well of Eternity collapsed during the Great Sundering, cataclysmic waves shattered the coastal city, toppling its grand marble arches and washing much of its stonework into the sea. The surviving night elves abandoned the ruined city in favor of smaller woodland villages further south, leaving Mathystra's sunken courtyards and cracked foundations to the relentless coastal elements.",["t"]="A City Cast into the Sea"},{["b"]="In the modern era, Mathystra has become a dangerous domain ruled by the Stormscale naga. Creeping up from the dark depths, these serpentine abominations guard the broken halls fiercely, driving away any travelers who venture north past the Tower of Althalaxx. Among the shattered flagstones, ancient Highborne relics still lie half-buried in sand and seafoam. Daring young night elves sometimes brave the naga vipers hoping to recover remnants of their lost heritage, often contending not only with serpent blades but also with the spectral Ghost Sabers that stalk the broken streets.",["t"]="The Stormscale Vipers and Ghost Sabers"}}}}}
t["subzone:ruins-of-ordil-aran"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,291,16.608.0,31.233.0,51.224.0,23.172.0,33.149.0",["h"]="07b0ef",["n"]="Las Ruinas de Ordil'Aran",["s"]="Las Ruinas de Ordil'Aran. Las Ruinas de Ordil'Aran son los vestigios derruidos de un antiguo asentamiento de elfos de la noche en el noroeste de Vallefresno, situado entre la Atalaya de Maestra y las Ruinas de Bathran. Antaño reducto oculto de cultores de las sombras, las piedras caídas han sido invadidas recientemente por los corruptos fúrbolgs Piel de Cardo. Poco queda de la arquitectura kaldorei original en Ordil'Aran, salvo pilares erosionados, arcos agrietados y mampostería cubierta de musgo. Durante un tiempo, las ruinas aisladas sirvieron de guarida para el Culto de la Facción Oscura, que acechaba entre los escombros para tender emboscadas a los viajeros por los senderos del noroeste de Vallefresno. Recientemente, sin embargo, los violentos fúrbolgs de la tribu Piel de Cardo expulsaron a los cultores en una sangrienta toma de control. Los cadáveres de los practicantes caídos de la Facción Oscura todavía cubren el suelo mientras fúrbolgs agresivos patrullan el perímetro, custodiando con fiereza el lugar y el antiguo árbol Duramen que crece en su interior.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Positioned just north of Maestra's Post, the aggressive occupants of Ordil'Aran threaten Alliance scouts and travelers heading toward Darkshore.",["race:NightElf"]="The ruins are another painful reminder of the Kalimdor empire's collapse, now defiled by corrupt furbolgs and dark cultists."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Ordil'Aran was an ancient night elf settlement dating back before the Great Sundering. Like many Kaldorei outposts across Ashenvale, it fell into decay over millennia, leaving behind only overgrown stone arches and crumbling masonry.",["al"]={"ordilaran history","what is ordil aran","who built ordil'aran"},["q"]="What was Ordil'Aran originally?"},{["a"]="The Cult of the Dark Strand previously used these ruins as a base of operations. The Thistlefur furbolgs violently attacked and ousted them, seizing the ruins for themselves and leaving slain cultists strewn across the site.",["al"]={"dead cultists","dark strand corpses","why are cultists dead here"},["q"]="Why are there dead cultists lying around the ruins?"},{["a"]="The Heartswood is a distinctive ancient tree growing within the Ruins of Ordil'Aran. Its branches and wood are sought after for their potent magical and natural properties.",["al"]={"heartswood tree","heartswood quest","heartswood ordil'aran"},["q"]="What is the Heartswood?"},{["a"]="The aggressive Thistlefur furbolgs currently occupy the ruins, having slain or driven out the Dark Strand cultists who previously inhabited the area.",["al"]={"who lives here","who is at ordil aran","ordilaran mobs"},["q"]="Who currently controls the ruins?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","cult of the dark strand","heartswood","maestra's post","ordil'aran","ordilaran","ruins","thistlefur"},["n"]="Ruins of Ordil'Aran",["s"]="The Ruins of Ordil'Aran are the crumbling remnants of an ancient night elf settlement in northwestern Ashenvale, situated between Maestra's Post and Bathran's Haunt. Once a hidden redoubt for shadow cultists, the fallen stones have recently been overrun by the corrupted Thistlefur furbolgs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Little remains of the original Kaldorei architecture at Ordil'Aran save for weathered pillars, cracked arches, and moss-draped stonework. For a time, the isolated ruins served as a lair for the Cult of the Dark Strand, who lurked among the debris to ambush travelers along the northwestern paths of Ashenvale. Recently, however, violent furbolgs of the Thistlefur tribe drove out the cultists in a bloody takeover. The bodies of fallen Dark Strand practitioners still litter the ground while aggressive furbolgs patrol the perimeter, fiercely guarding the site and the ancient Heartswood tree growing within.",["t"]="A Contested Ruin"}}}}}
t["subzone:ruins-of-stardust"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,400,20.409.0,21.391.0,52.222.0,46.201.0,39.232.0,32.212.0",["h"]="828a4d",["n"]="Las Ruinas del Polvo Estelar",["s"]="Las Ruinas del Polvo Estelar. Las ruinas del Polvo Estelar son un antiguo santuario sagrado de los elfos de la noche en ruinas, enclavado en una isla lacustre en el suroeste de Vallefresno. Antaño un sereno lugar de devoción, las aguas de la isla y las bestias del pantano autóctonas han sufrido la corrupción procedente de la podredumbre demoníaca que desciende de Frondavil. A pesar de esta plaga omnipresente, los luminosos arbustos de polvo estelar todavía prosperan entre las piedras derruidas, conservando un potente poder restaurador. Ubicadas en una isla solitaria al sur de Astranaar, Las ruinas del Polvo Estelar fueron antaño un venerado lugar sagrado de los elfos de la noche. Hoy en día, un tono verdoso amarillento, inquietante y enfermizo, se cierne sobre el agua; una consecuencia de la inmunda podredumbre demoníaca que drena hacia el sur desde Frondavil, de forma muy parecida a lo que ocurre en el cercano Lago Iris. La flora local ha mutado en hostiles bestias del pantano que merodean por los restos de mampostería caídos, con sus temperamentos alterados por el lago contaminado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="The uncorrupted stardust found here serves as a vital cleansing reagent during spiritual trials, including the vital Call of Water trials to master the restorative elements.",["race:NightElf"]="Watching this former sanctuary succumb to Felwood's slow, putrid runoff is a painful reminder of the ongoing struggle to protect Ashenvale from enduring demonic corruption."},["faq"]={{["a"]="In ancient times, the site was a sacred holy ground tended by the night elves. Its classical marble pillars and lakeside perch served as a tranquil place of reverence long before demonic corruption took root in the forest.",["al"]={"what are the ruins","stardust lore","who built stardust"},["q"]="What were the Ruins of Stardust originally used for?"},{["a"]="Demonic corruption seeping down from the blighted peaks of Felwood into Ashenvale's waterways has tainted the lake, tinting the waters a murky, yellowish-green shade and disturbing the natural balance.",["al"]={"why is water green","why is the lake corrupted","stardust water"},["q"]="Why is the water around the island discolored?"},{["a"]="Despite growing in soil soaked in demonic runoff, stardust shrubs remain completely pure. They resist the ambient taint and possess exceptional restorative and healing properties, making them valuable reagents for cleansing rituals.",["al"]={"what is stardust shrub","stardust plant","stardust bushes"},["q"]="What makes the stardust shrubs special?"},{["a"]="The island is overrun by large, corrupted bog beasts. The lake's tainted water has warped these nature elementals from peaceful forest guardians into aggressive, lumbering threats to anyone crossing the shallows.",["al"]={"stardust mobs","what monsters are here","bog beasts"},["q"]="What creatures wander the ruins?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","bog beasts","felwood taint","night elf ruins","ruins of stardust","stardust shrubs","water corruption"},["n"]="Ruins of Stardust",["s"]="The Ruins of Stardust are an ancient, fallen night elven holy sanctuary nestled on a lake island in southwestern Ashenvale. Once a serene place of worship, the island's waters and native bog beasts have suffered corruption from demonic rot washing down from Felwood. Despite this pervasive blight, luminous stardust shrubs still thrive amidst the crumbling stones, retaining potent restorative power.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Resting on a solitary island south of Astranaar, the Ruins of Stardust were once a venerated night elf holy site. Today, an eerie, sickly yellowish-green hue hangs over the water—a consequence of foul demonic rot draining south from Felwood, much like at nearby Iris Lake. The local plant life has twisted into hostile bog beasts that prowl the fallen masonry, their temperaments warped by the tainted lake.",["t"]="A Blighted Sanctuary"},{["b"]="Despite the corruption saturating the soil and shoreline, the island possesses an unyielding spark of resilience. Scattered among the ruins are stardust shrubs, blooming unmarred by the demonic taint. Their leaves and blossoms hold remarkable cleansing and healing virtues, attracting shamans, herbalists, and local night elf defenders seeking remedies against Ashenvale's encroaching decay.",["t"]="The Enduring Stardust"}}}}}
t["subzone:rut-theran-village"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,232,25.597.0,36.205.0,37.144.0,64.242.0,29.199.0",["h"]="9fff4f",["n"]="Aldea Rut'theran",["s"]="Aldea Rut'theran. Aldea Rut'theran es un refugio costero enclavado en la base sur de Teldrassil. Al servir como el principal puerto marítimo de Darnassus, conecta el aislado Árbol del Mundo con el continente de Kalimdor mediante rutas de ferry e hipogrifos. Encaramada a la orilla del agua, bajo las imponentes alturas de Teldrassil, Aldea Rut'theran actúa como el umbral entre la capital de los elfos de la noche y el resto del mundo. Mientras que Darnassus reposa entre las ramas en lo alto, Rut'theran proporciona la base logística necesaria para sustentarla. Un portal místico se alza bajo los árboles, transportando en un instante a los viajeros entre la orilla y Darnassus. Para los viajes a través del mar, un servicio de ferry opera desde los muelles de la aldea directamente hasta Auberdine, en la costa continental de Costa Oscura, acompañado de maestros de vuelo que cuidan de posaderos exclusivos de hipogrifos adiestrados.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Druids passing through Rut'theran Village can catch hippogryph flights directly across northern Kalimdor to the sacred sanctuary of Moonglade.",["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves leaving Teldrassil to aid the Alliance, Rut'theran Village is the final farewell to the crown of the World Tree before sailing into mainland Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Walk up the gentle slope from the docks toward the giant pavilion tent. Stepping directly into the glowing purple portal on the platform will instantly transport you to the Temple Gardens inside Darnassus.",["al"]={"get to darnassus","portal to darnassus","how to reach darnassus"},["q"]="How do I get to Darnassus from here?"},{["a"]="The ship docked at Rut'theran Village, the Moonspray, provides passage across the Veiled Sea to the town of Auberdine on the coast of Darkshore.",["al"]={"where does boat go","rut'theran ferry","ruttheran ship route"},["q"]="Where does the boat from the dock go?"},{["a"]="Teldrassil's canopy is far too elevated for conventional sailing ships or sea trade. Rut'theran Village was established at its roots to provide a sea-level port and roosting ground, linked to the heights via a permanent teleportation gateway.",["al"]={"why is ruttheran at sea level","why bottom of teldrassil"},["q"]="Why is this village down at sea level instead of up in the tree?"},{["a"]="Yes. A hippogryph handler operates from the village roost, offering flight routes across the water to Auberdine in Darkshore, as well as specialized transport for Cenarion Circle druids to Moonglade.",["al"]={"rut'theran flight path","where can hippogryph fly"},["q"]="Can I fly anywhere from here?"}},["kw"]={"auberdine","darkshore","darnassus","docks","hippogryph","moonspray","port","rut'theran","teldrassil"},["n"]="Rut'theran Village",["s"]="Rut'theran Village is a coastal haven nestled at the southern base of Teldrassil. Serving as the primary maritime harbor for Darnassus, it connects the secluded World Tree to the mainland of Kalimdor via ferry and hippogryph routes.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched at the water's edge below the towering heights of Teldrassil, Rut'theran Village acts as the threshold between the night elven capital and the wider world. While Darnassus rests within the boughs high above, Rut'theran provides the logistical foundation required to sustain it. A mystical portal arches beneath the trees, whisking travelers between the shore and Darnassus in an instant. For journeys across the sea, ferry service runs from the village docks directly to Auberdine on the mainland of Darkshore, accompanied by flight masters tending dedicated roosts of trained hippogryphs.",["t"]="Gateway to the World Tree"}}}}}
t["subzone:saldean-s-farm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,249,20.398.0,16.415.0,53.267.0,49.228.0,47.189.0,42.204.0",["h"]="80d2a3",["n"]="Finca de Saldean",["s"]="Finca de Saldean. La Finca de Saldean es el único hogar de Páramos de Poniente que no ha sido invadido por completo y abandonado ante la Hermandad Defias. Mantenida por el testarudo Granjero Saldean y su esposa Salma, la granja sigue siendo un refugio seguro poco común en medio de la agitación de la región. Mientras las tierras vecinas sucumbían al bandidaje y al sabotaje mecánico, la familia Saldean se negó a abandonar sus tierras. El Granjero Saldean y su esposa Salma han permanecido en su propiedad, ofreciendo comida caliente y palabras amables a los viajeros que pasan. A pesar de su resistencia, los campos continúan asolados por gólems de la cosecha rebeldes desplegados por las llanuras, lo que obliga a la familia a permanecer cerca de los muros de la granja.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Saldean's Farm represents the raw, failing edge of the kingdom's frontier, exposing how deeply ordinary citizens suffer when Stormwind's leadership is distracted.",["profession:Cooking"]="Salma Saldean is renowned among travelers for turning scavenged Westfall ingredients into hearty, lifesaving dishes like Goretusk Liver Pie."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Farmer Saldean and his wife simply refused to pack up and flee when the Defias Brotherhood swept through Westfall. Though hostile harvest golems prowl their crops, the family stubbornly defends the immediate perimeter with the help of passing militia and adventurers.",["al"]={"why not overrun","saldean farm survival","how is the farm alive"},["q"]="Why is this farm still standing when the others fell?"},{["a"]="The farm's residents are Farmer Saldean and his wife Salma; anyone else you find there is likely a passing traveler, as the couple welcome visitors and the adventurers willing to help them with the dangers plaguing their fields.",["al"]={"refugees at saldean","homeless westfall","orphans at farm"},["q"]="Who are all the people gathered around the house?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood repurposed the region's mechanical harvest reapers and golems into deadly sentries. They roam the fields attacking anyone who attempts to cultivate or clear the land.",["al"]={"harvest golems","why are robots in crops","mechanical scarecrows"},["q"]="Why are mechanical golems attacking the fields?"},{["a"]="Official military presence is practically nonexistent. A few scattered guards from Sentinel Hill and Stormwind provide minimal watch, but the crown has largely left Westfall's defense to local initiative.",["al"]={"stormwind military presence","sentinel hill guards here","guard support"},["q"]="Is the Stormwind Army protecting the farm?"}},["kw"]={"farmer saldean","halfway house","harvest golem","refugees","saldean","salma saldean","westfall"},["n"]="Saldean's Farm",["s"]="Saldean's Farm is the only homestead in Westfall that has not been completely overrun and abandoned to the Defias Brotherhood. Held by the stubborn Farmer Saldean and his wife Salma, the farmhouse remains a rare safe haven amid the region's turmoil.",["sec"]={{["b"]="While neighboring lands fell to banditry and mechanical sabotage, the Saldean family refused to abandon their soil. Farmer Saldean and his wife Salma have stayed on their homestead, offering hot food and a kind word to passing travelers. Despite their resilience, the fields remain plagued by rogue harvest golems deployed across the plains, forcing the family to stay close to the farmhouse walls.",["t"]="A Beacon in the Dust"},{["b"]="Because the Stormwind crown has largely neglected Westfall, law enforcement here is thin. A handful of Sentinel Hill and Stormwind guards patrol the periphery, but the farm survives primarily through sheer grit and the aid of passing travelers. For the Saldeans, Salma's famous Westfall stew and goretusk liver pie and the shelter of their farmhouse are small comforts against the ever-present threat of the Defias.",["t"]="Holding the Line"}}}}}
t["subzone:satyrnaar"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,298,23.645.0,18.184.0,23.158.0,59.172.0,46.144.0",["h"]="d70378",["n"]="Satyrnaar",["s"]="Satyrnaar. Satyrnaar es un antiguo asentamiento en ruinas de los elfos de la noche situado en el noreste de Vallefresno que ha caído por completo en manos de los sátiros Bleakheart. Emplazado justo al lado del camino principal entre el Puesto del Hachazo y Azshara, es el más intacto y de más fácil acceso de los bastiones de sátiros del bosque. Ubicado al noreste del Puesto del Hachazo y al suroeste de Canción del Bosque, Satyrnaar se erige como uno de los tres asentamientos principales de sátiros de Vallefresno junto a Xavian y la Senda de la Noche. A diferencia de las ruinas más adentradas en la espesura, Satyrnaar está relativamente bien conservado, con tiendas montadas entre la derruida arquitectura élfica. Sirve como un concurrido campamento para los sátiros Bleakheart, haciendo que la ruta comercial cercana esté plagada de peligros para los viajeros que van hacia el este rumbo a Azshara. Además, aquí se fraguan oscuros vínculos: los sátiros han forjado una alianza con el sombrío Culto de la Facción Oscura, albergando una de sus insidiosas gemas de alma entre las piedras corruptas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The twisted fel corruption spread by the Bleakheart satyrs actively chokes the natural spirit of Ashenvale, demanding swift cleansing.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing ancestral stonework defiled by fel corruption and inhabited by the cursed remnants of the Highborne is a bitter offense to any night elf traveling through Ashenvale."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Satyrnaar is a ruined night elf site in northeastern Ashenvale that has been claimed and occupied by the Bleakheart satyrs. It serves as one of their primary strongholds in the region.",["al"]={"satyrnaar overview","what is this place","satyr camp"},["q"]="What is Satyrnaar?"},{["a"]="The settlement is held by the Bleakheart tribe of satyrs. They have erected tents among the ancient ruins and work in league with the Cult of the Dark Strand.",["al"]={"who is here","satyrnaar mobs","bleakheart satyrs"},["q"]="Who lives in Satyrnaar?"},{["a"]="Of the three main satyr sites in Ashenvale—Satyrnaar, Night Run, and Xavian—Satyrnaar is the most intact and centrally located, lying right off the road toward Azshara.",["al"]={"satyrnaar vs xavian","why satyrnaar"},["q"]="Why is Satyrnaar significant compared to other satyr ruins?"},{["a"]="Satyrnaar houses one of the corrupted soulgems belonging to the Cult of the Dark Strand, a mortal shadow cult allied with the Bleakheart satyrs.",["al"]={"dark strand soulgem","satyrnaar crystal","soulgem"},["q"]="What is the dark artifact hidden in Satyrnaar?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","bleakheart","dark strand","forest song","satyr","satyrnaar","soulgem","splintertree"},["n"]="Satyrnaar",["s"]="Satyrnaar is an ancient, ruined night elf settlement in northeastern Ashenvale that has fallen entirely into the hands of the Bleakheart satyrs. Perched just off the main road between Splintertree Post and Azshara, it is the most intact and easily accessible of the satyr strongholds in the forest.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located northeast of Splintertree Post and southwest of Forest Song, Satyrnaar stands as one of Ashenvale's three primary satyr settlements alongside Xavian and Night Run. Unlike the deeper wilderness ruins, Satyrnaar is relatively well-preserved, featuring pitched tents nestled among crumbled elven architecture. It serves as a bustling camp for the Bleakheart satyrs, making the nearby trade route fraught with peril for travelers moving east toward Azshara. Furthermore, dark ties fester here: the satyrs have forged an alliance with the shadowy Cult of the Dark Strand, harboring one of their insidious soulgems amidst the corrupted stones.",["t"]="A Den of Fel and Shadow"}}}}}
t["subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="20,330,12.576.0,24.516.1,34.117.0,41.266.0,38.153.0,63.184.0",["h"]="d8e184",["n"]="Mesón del Cuervo Escarlata",["s"]="Mesón del Cuervo Escarlata. El Mesón del Cuervo Escarlata es el centro social y la posada principal de Villa Oscura, y ofrece un refugio junto al fuego en la penumbra de Bosque del Ocaso. Regentada por el tabernero Smitts, sirve como punto de encuentro para lugareños asediados, aventureros de paso y viajeros aterrorizados que intentan escapar de los horrores que acechan más allá de los límites de la villa. Situado cerca del corazón de Villa Oscura, el Mesón del Cuervo Escarlata mantiene su hogar encendido mientras un anochecer eterno asfixia el bosque circundante. Años atrás, era una parada bulliciosa donde el alguacil Haggard y la Guardia de Ventormenta compartían pintas tras las patrullas. Hoy en día, el negocio ha menguado a la par que la seguridad del pueblo. El tabernero Smitts atiende la barra para una clientela sombría y ansiosa que se acurruca contra el frío y el miedo. Aun así, la taberna sigue siendo una encrucijada indispensable para los rumores, sirviendo como punto de partida para los viajeros que buscan respuestas a los oscuros fenómenos que consumen la región.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers traversing the southern border, the Scarlet Raven provides one of the few safe hearths and rest stops between Elwynn Forest and Deadwind Pass.",["profession:Cooking"]="The inn's menu features regional delicacies like Dusky Crab Cakes, a local staple that desperate wanderers like Jitters crave even while hiding in the graveyard."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Tavernkeep Smitts is the tavern keeper. The inn also has an innkeeper and other staff serving travelers in Darkshire.",["al"]={"innkeeper of darkshire","who owns the scarlet raven","tavernkeep smitts"},["q"]="Who runs the Scarlet Raven Tavern?"},{["a"]="The curse hanging over Duskwood has choked the trade routes and terrified the locals. With undead, feral worgen, and shadowy riders prowling the woods outside, the patron crowd consists of terrified townsfolk and desperate mercenaries rather than carefree travelers.",["al"]={"why is scarlet raven depressing","darkshire inn atmosphere"},["q"]="Why is the tavern's atmosphere so gloomy?"},{["a"]="Jitters stayed at the tavern and frantically wrote in his journal before fleeing town. His reasons are uncovered through the investigation into Duskwood.",["al"]={"jitters room","jitters tavern","did jitters live here"},["q"]="Did Jitters stay at the Scarlet Raven?"},{["a"]="Old patrons and past town records preserved in and around the tavern hold clues regarding Stalvan Mistmantle, who once frequented the settlement before falling into tragedy and infamy.",["al"]={"stalvan inn connection","stalvan mistmantle darkshire inn"},["q"]="What connection does this tavern have to the Legend of Stalvan?"}},["kw"]={"darkshire","duskwood","dusky crab cakes","haggard","jitters","scarlet raven","smitts","tavernkeep smitts"},["n"]="Scarlet Raven Tavern",["s"]="The Scarlet Raven Tavern is the social center and primary inn of Darkshire, offering hearthside shelter in the gloom of Duskwood. Presided over by Tavernkeep Smitts, it serves as a gathering spot for beleaguered locals, passing adventurers, and terrified travelers trying to escape the horrors lurking beyond the town's perimeter.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing near the heart of Darkshire, the Scarlet Raven Tavern keeps its hearth ablaze while eternal dusk chokes the surrounding forest. Years ago, it was a bustling stop where Marshal Haggard and the Stormwind Guard would share pints after patrols. Today, business has withered alongside the town's security. Tavernkeep Smitts tends bar for a somber, anxious clientele huddled against the cold and fear. Even so, the tavern remains an indispensable crossroads for rumors, serving as the starting point for travelers seeking answers to the dark phenomena consuming the region.",["t"]="A Dim Refuge"},{["b"]="Beyond serving as a shelter, the tavern holds pieces of several unfolding mysteries. The reclusive wanderer Jitters rented a room here for days, frantically scribbling in his journal by night before fleeing town ahead of the terrifying Dark Riders. Decades-old town gossip and preserved guest records kept beneath its roof also link back to long-forgotten figures like Stalvan Mistmantle, making Smitts' taproom the first place inquisitive investigators search when tracing the histories of Duskwood's restless dead.",["t"]="Secrets and Stolen Pints"}}}}}
t["subzone:scarlet-watch-post"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,297,30.721.0,46.327.0,36.192.0,66.241.0",["h"]="66fe06",["n"]="Atalaya Escarlata",["s"]="Atalaya Escarlata. La Atalaya Escarlata es una torre de vigilancia aislada situada en las colinas rocosas del noreste de Claros de Tirisfal, justo al norte del Monasterio Escarlata. Mantenida por una vigilante guarnición de cruzados, su único propósito es proteger el vulnerable flanco norte del monasterio contra ataques por el flanco. Encaramada en las escarpadas alturas tras el Monasterio Escarlata, la Atalaya Escarlata sirve como un bastión crucial de alerta temprana para los fanáticos de abajo. Mientras que el camino del sur hacia la puerta del monasterio cuenta con gran tráfico y fortificaciones, los escarpados acantilados a lo largo de la costa norte de Tirisfal ofrecen una tentadora ruta trasera para los infiltrados. Para eliminar este punto ciego, La Cruzada Escarlata mantiene esta torre de piedra fortificada, uno de los varios puestos avanzados de cruzados dispersos por Claros de Tirisfal. Bajo el severo mando del capitán Melrache, una fuerza combinada de neófitos, vanguardistas y devotos frailes mantiene una vigilancia incesante sobre los acantilados, asegurando que ni la Plaga ni los Renegados puedan sorprender a la orden por la espalda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The Crusaders view all outsiders—living or dead—as tainted carriers of undeath, making this watch post strictly hostile ground to any Horde travelers braving the hills.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Scarlet Crusade is an existential threat lingering right on the Undercity's doorstep; purging isolated towers like this disrupts the zealots' communication network and secures northern Tirisfal."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The outpost protects the Scarlet Monastery from being flanked. While the monastery's main entrance faces south toward the Tirisfal roads, its rear slopes toward the northern wilderness, leaving it vulnerable to coordinated assaults. The watch post ensures sentries spot and intercept any intruders attempting a northern bypass.",["al"]={"why is scarlet watch post here","scarlet watch post purpose","crusaders run role"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Scarlet Watch Post?"},{["a"]="Captain Melrache oversees the garrison stationed at the tower. He commands a defensive retinue including personal bodyguards, front-line Vanguards, aspiring Neophytes, and spellcasting Friars.",["al"]={"scarlet watch post leader","who leads scarlet watch post","captain melrache"},["q"]="Who commands the Scarlet Watch Post?"},{["a"]="Yes. It is one of four distinct Crusader outposts ringing the northern and western reaches of Tirisfal Glades. These stone towers create a defensive perimeter to monitor Scourge activity and contain the Forsaken expansion from the Undercity.",["al"]={"tirisfal towers","crusader outposts tirisfal","other scarlet towers"},["q"]="Is the Scarlet Watch Post related to the other towers in Tirisfal?"}},["kw"]={"captain melrache","crusader outpost","crusader's run","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","scarlet watch post","tirisfal glades"},["n"]="Scarlet Watch Post",["s"]="The Scarlet Watch Post is an isolated watchtower stationed in the rocky hills of northeastern Tirisfal Glades, just north of the Scarlet Monastery. Maintained by a vigilant garrison of Crusaders, its sole purpose is to safeguard the monastery's vulnerable northern flank against flanking assaults.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched in the rugged heights behind the Scarlet Monastery, the Scarlet Watch Post serves as a critical early-warning bastion for the zealots below. While the southern road up to the monastery gate receives heavy traffic and fortifications, the rugged cliffs along Tirisfal's northern coastline provide a tempting back route for infiltrators. To eliminate this blind spot, the Scarlet Crusade maintains this fortified stone tower—one of several Crusader outposts scattered across Tirisfal Glades. Under the stern command of Captain Melrache, a mixed force of Neophytes, Vanguards, and devout Friars keeps ceaseless vigil over the cliffs, ensuring neither the Scourge nor the Forsaken can surprise the order from behind.",["t"]="Guarding the Northern Approach"}}}}}
t["subzone:screaming-gully"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,265,26.511.0,37.165.0,37.209.0,35.145.0,33.162.0",["h"]="866f10",["n"]="Barranco de los Gritos",["s"]="Barranco de los Gritos. El Barranco de los Gritos es la primera y vasta caverna subterránea que se encuentra justo tras la entrada de las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Bañada por un brillo fúngico antinatural y aguas poco profundas, sirve como reducto exterior para los corruptos Druidas del Colmillo y sus bestias mutadas. Cruzar el umbral de las Cuevas de los Lamentos conduce directamente al Barranco de los Gritos, un abismo resonante donde el viento gime a través de fisuras subterráneas. Lejos de los áridos Baldíos de la superficie, la quebrada está asfixiada por una vegetación húmeda, niebla sofocante y una fauna agresiva retorcida por la Pesadilla Esmeralda. La noble del Colmillo Lady Anacondra vigila la cámara, rodeada de acólitos de los Druidas del Colmillo y feroces raptores descarriados, mientras antiguas tortugas mordedoras como Kresh patrullan las aguas someras inferiores.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion druids, Screaming Gully is a heartbreaking display of their fallen brethren who abandoned the path of the claw and sky to embrace serpentine corruption."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Screaming Gully is the first major chamber you enter directly after stepping through the portal inside the Wailing Caverns, located beneath the northern Barrens.",["al"]={"screaming gully location","where is screaming gully","how to find screaming gully"},["q"]="Where is the Screaming Gully located?"},{["a"]="The Wailing Caverns earn their name from the howling, moaning sounds caused by subterranean steam and winds venting through rock fissures, and this wide entrance chasm catches the brunt of those echoing cries.",["al"]={"why screaming gully","screaming gully name origin"},["q"]="Why is it called the Screaming Gully?"},{["a"]="The chamber is overseen by Lady Anacondra, one of the primary Fanglords who fell under the corruption of the Emerald Nightmare alongside Naralex.",["al"]={"screaming gully boss","who is in screaming gully","screaming gully leader"},["q"]="Who rules over the Screaming Gully?"},{["a"]="The gully is populated by deviate raptors, corrupted Druids of the Fang, and wandering aquatic life, including the ancient turtle Kresh roaming the flooded floor.",["al"]={"screaming gully mobs","enemies in screaming gully"},["q"]="What creatures roam this chamber?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","deviate raptor","fanglords","kresh","lady anacondra","screaming gully","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Screaming Gully",["s"]="Screaming Gully is the first sprawling subterranean cavern encountered just beyond the entrance of the Wailing Caverns. Bathed in unnatural fungal glow and shallow waters, it serves as the outer redoubt for the corrupted Druids of the Fang and their mutated beasts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stepping through the threshold of the Wailing Caverns leads directly into Screaming Gully, an echoing chasm where the wind groans through subterranean fissures. Far from the arid Barrens above, the gully is choked with damp overgrowth, humid mist, and aggressive wildlife twisted by the Emerald Nightmare. The Fanglord Lady Anacondra oversees the chamber, surrounded by acolytes of the Druids of the Fang and vicious deviate raptors, while ancient snapping turtles like Kresh patrol the shallow waterways below.",["t"]="Threshold of the Nightmare"}}}}}
t["subzone:scuttle-coast"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,315,21.634.0,20.450.0,41.229.0,35.198.0,46.153.0,36.187.0",["h"]="082665",["n"]="Costa de la Huída",["s"]="Costa de la Huída. La Costa de la Huída es la costa oriental de Durotar, azotada por las olas y situada entre Cerrotajo y el Fuerte de Tiragarde. La playa rocosa está sembrada de restos hundidos de la flota de Kul Tiras del almirante Daelin Valiente, lo que la convierte en una activa zona de rescate para la Horda y un constante recordatorio de la reciente guerra naval. Extendiéndose a lo largo del extremo oriental de Durotar hacia el Mare Magnum, la Costa de la Huída adquirió su sombrío carácter durante la invasión liderada por el Gran Almirante Daelin Valiente. Cuando la flota de Kul Tiras asaltó la incipiente nación de Durotar, las encarnizadas batallas con la Horda arrojaron muchos buques de guerra humanos contra los escarpados bajíos, destrozándolos y reduciéndolos a cascos astillados. Hoy en día, la costa está abarrotada de maderas cubiertas de percebes, jarcias rotas y barriles de carga recuperados. Para los campamentos cercanos de Cerrotajo, la costa representa tanto un persistente peligro para la seguridad como una valiosa fuente de provisiones recuperadas y mecanismos abandonados de la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The broken hulls littering this beach stand as stark monuments to Durotar's defense against Daelin Proudmoore's invading navy.",["profession:Engineering"]="The sunken Alliance holds along the shore contain abandoned gnomish gadgets, scrap metal, and intricate machinery ripe for reverse-engineering."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The shattered ships belonged to the naval fleet of Kul Tiras under Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. They were smashed against Durotar's rocky shallows during the admiral's failed military campaign against the newly founded Horde.",["al"]={"why are there ships here","who owns the wrecked ships","sunken ships durotar"},["q"]="Where did all these shipwrecks come from?"},{["a"]="The name carries a double meaning. It refers directly to the warships scuttled along the coastline during naval combat, as well as the numerous makrura and crabs that scuttle across the rocky sands.",["al"]={"why is it called scuttle coast","scuttle coast name origin"},["q"]="Why is it called the Scuttle Coast?"},{["a"]="Horde scouts and scavengers search the broken holds for salvageable tools, supplies, and discarded gnomish technology left behind by the Alliance forces.",["al"]={"what are orcs salvaging","horde salvage scuttle coast"},["q"]="What is the Horde looking for along the coast?"},{["a"]="No. Aside from treacherous waves and jagged rocks, hostile coastal beasts like makrura prowl the surf, and armed Kul Tiras survivors remain entrenched just to the south at Tiragarde Keep.",["al"]={"scuttle coast dangers","is scuttle coast dangerous"},["q"]="Is the Scuttle Coast safe to travel?"}},["kw"]={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","kul tiras","makrura","razor hill","scuttle coast","shipwrecks","tiragarde keep"},["n"]="Scuttle Coast",["s"]="The Scuttle Coast is the wave-battered eastern shoreline of Durotar, situated between Razor Hill and Tiragarde Keep. The rocky beach is strewn with sunken wreckage from Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet, making it an active scavenging ground for the Horde and a lingering reminder of recent naval warfare.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Running along Durotar's eastern edge out to the Great Sea, the Scuttle Coast earned its grim character during the invasion led by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. When the Kul Tiras fleet assaulted the fledgling nation of Durotar, fierce battles with the Horde drove many human warships against the jagged shoals, smashing them into splintered hulks. Today, the shoreline is choked with barnacle-encrusted timber, broken rigging, and salvaged cargo barrels. For the nearby encampments of Razor Hill, the coast represents both a lingering security hazard and a valuable source of recovered provisions and abandoned Alliance mechanisms.",["t"]="Wreckage of the Fleet"},{["b"]="The name Scuttle Coast refers not only to the sunken warships deliberately scuttled or grounded during the fighting, but also to the swarms of crabs and makrura that pick through the rotting detritus. While shoreline wildlife and dangerous tides keep casual travelers away, Horde scavengers periodically comb through the wreckage to retrieve valuable equipment, including gnomish technical components abandoned in the cargo holds of the sunken ships.",["t"]="Scavengers and Tides"}}}}}
t["subzone:sen-jin-village"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,393,15.634.0,17.569.0,49.282.0,16.271.0,53.258.0,50.247.0",["h"]="e97130",["n"]="Poblado Sen'jin",["s"]="Poblado Sen'jin. El Poblado Sen'jin es un asentamiento costero en la costa sur de Durotar que sirve de santuario para los trols Lanza Negra. Fundada por el Jefe Vol'jin tras ser expulsado su pueblo de su hogar ancestral en las Islas del Eco, la aldea rinde homenaje a su difunto padre, el médico brujo Sen'jin. Hoy se erige como un frágil refugio centrado en la supervivencia, la herboristería y la recuperación de lo que les fue arrebatado. Cuando el oscuro médico brujo Zalazane traicionó a los Lanza Negra y se hizo con el control de las Islas del Eco, el Jefe Vol'jin se vio obligado a guiar a los supervivientes a través del estrecho hasta el continente de Durotar. Allí, al abrigo de los acantilados costeros y con la vista puesta en el mar, levantaron toscas chozas y fundaron el Poblado Sen'jin. El asentamiento lleva el nombre del padre de Vol'jin, el venerable anciano que se sacrificó durante la Tercera Guerra para salvar a su pueblo de los múrlocs costeros. A pesar de su estrecha alianza con la Horda de Thrall, los trols de aquí viven bajo la sombra del exilio, contemplando a diario desde los bajíos el hogar que perdieron.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Herbalism"]="The village is a vital starting center for natural medicine, surrounded by coastal Peacebloom, Silverleaf, and Earthroot used by local witch doctors to treat venom and curses.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls emerging from the Valley of Trials, this refuge is the beating heart of their displaced people, holding memories of their lost chieftain and the enduring sting of Zalazane's betrayal."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Darkspear fled across the strait to the Durotar coastline after the witch doctor Zalazane went mad and took control of their home on the Echo Isles. Sen'jin Village was established by Vol'jin as a temporary refuge and staging ground just across the water from their stolen land.",["al"]={"why is senjin village here","why are trolls in durotar","why did trolls leave echo isles"},["q"]="Why did the Darkspear build Sen'jin Village here?"},{["a"]="Sen'jin was a respected witch doctor and chieftain of the Darkspear tribe, as well as the father of Vol'jin. During the Third War, he foresaw Thrall's arrival and sacrificed his life while saving his tribe and the young Horde from fanatical sea murlocs in the South Seas.",["al"]={"who was senjin","who is senjin named after","senjin lore"},["q"]="Who was Sen'jin?"},{["a"]="The local witch doctors and medicine men rely heavily on Durotar's coastal flora and scorpok venoms to concoct charms, antidotes, and rituals. These botanical brews sustain the wounded and offer wards against the dark hexes drifting over from the Echo Isles.",["al"]={"senjin village trainers","professions in senjin village","why alchemy here"},["q"]="Why are there so many herbalists and alchemists here?"},{["a"]="The Echo Isles sit directly across the eastern water from the village. Adventurers often swim or wade across the shallow channel to strike back at Zalazane's voodoo cultists, recover stolen artifacts, or gather resources for the village defenders.",["al"]={"how to get to echo isles","isles off senjin coast","swimming to echo isles"},["q"]="Can you reach the Echo Isles from Sen'jin Village?"}},["kw"]={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","senjin","vol'jin","zalazane"},["n"]="Sen'jin Village",["s"]="Sen'jin Village is a coastal settlement on the southern shores of Durotar, serving as a sanctuary for the Darkspear trolls. Established by Chieftain Vol'jin after his people were driven from their ancestral home on the Echo Isles, the hamlet honors his fallen father, the witch doctor Sen'jin. Today, it stands as a fragile haven focused on survival, herbalism, and reclaiming what was stolen.",["sec"]={{["b"]="When the dark witch doctor Zalazane betrayed the Darkspear and seized control of the Echo Isles, Chieftain Vol'jin was forced to lead the survivors across the strait to the mainland of Durotar. There, nestled beneath coastal cliffs and looking out over the water, they raised crude huts and established Sen'jin Village. The settlement carries the name of Vol'jin's father, the venerable elder who sacrificed himself during the Third War to save their people from coastal murlocs. Despite their close alliance with Thrall's Horde, the trolls here live under the shadow of exile, staring daily across the shallows at the home they lost.",["t"]="A Refugee Shore"},{["b"]="Daily life in Sen'jin Village revolves around preparation and defense. Between local Centaur raids, aggressive sea beasts, and Zalazane's hexes reaching across the sea, the villagers rely heavily on herbal remedies and brewing potent alchemical spirits. While Vol'jin coordinates broader tribal defense from the Horde capital, local shamans, hunters, and scouts gather here to recruit fresh wanderers stepping out of the Valley of Trials. Their aim is clear: to gather resources, protect Durotar's southern flank, and plot the eventual downfall of the traitor Zalazane.",["t"]="Eyes on the Isles"}}}}}
t["subzone:sentinel-hill"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,276,21.516.0,20.514.0,59.292.0,34.253.0,40.211.0,47.234.0",["h"]="2f6be6",["n"]="Colina del Centinela",["s"]="Colina del Centinela. La Colina del Centinela es el bastión principal de la Alianza en Páramos de Poniente y sirve como centro de mando para Las Milicias del Pueblo. Rodeada de campos descuidados, gnolls carroñeros y forajidos hostiles, esta elevación fortificada es el único punto de apoyo seguro para los ciudadanos leales de la región. Encaramada en una posición elevada en el centro de Páramos de Poniente, la Colina del Centinela se erige como un santuario vital en un territorio sumido en la anarquía. Cuenta con una posada tipo barracón, un nido de grifos que conecta a los viajeros con Ventormenta y más allá, una forja y un aserradero, todo ello anclado por la imponente Torre del Centinela. Mientras las tierras circundantes han caído presa del bandidaje y de bestias voraces, el campamento mantiene un frágil perímetro donde viajeros, granjeros asediados y reclutas pueden reagruparse bajo la atenta mirada de veteranos defensores.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Sentinel Hill is your only fortified outpost and supply hub in Westfall, anchoring the Alliance's presence against outlaws and raiders.",["race:Human"]="Seeing Westfall's farmers forced to raise their own militia here reflects the kingdom's deepening crisis while the throne remains vacant."},["faq"]={{["a"]="With King Varian Wrynn missing and resources spread thin across the realm, Stormwind's regency has largely abandoned the western provinces to their own devices. Local citizens and veterans had to form the People's Militia themselves to hold Sentinel Hill and protect what remains of Westfall.",["al"]={"why no stormwind guards","where is stormwind army","why militia here"},["q"]="Why hasn't Stormwind sent soldiers to defend Sentinel Hill?"},{["a"]="Gryan Stoutmantle commands the People's Militia from the base of Sentinel Tower. He coordinates local defense, gathers intelligence on surrounding threats, and directs visiting adventurers against the gnolls and highwaymen encroaching on the settlement.",["al"]={"who leads sentinel hill","sentinel hill commander","gryan stoutmantle"},["q"]="Who is in charge of Sentinel Hill?"},{["a"]="The encampment faces constant pressure from aggressive Riverpaw gnolls roaming the western plains, as well as the insidious, coordinated sabotage of the Defias Brotherhood lurking throughout the abandoned farms.",["al"]={"what attacks sentinel hill","sentinel hill enemies","who is attacking"},["q"]="What threats actively endanger the hill?"},{["a"]="Sentinel Hill provides a full set of frontier accommodations: a gryphon master offering travel to Stormwind City and other Alliance outposts, an innkeeper, a mailbox, trade supply vendors, and repair facilities around the local forge.",["al"]={"sentinel hill amenities","sentinel hill flight path","is there an inn here"},["q"]="What services are available here for travelers?"}},["kw"]={"gryan stoutmantle","gryphon roost","peoples militia","riverpaw gnolls","sentinel hill","sentinel tower","westfall"},["n"]="Sentinel Hill",["s"]="Sentinel Hill is the primary bastion of the Alliance in Westfall, serving as the command center for the People's Militia. Surrounded by overgrown fields, scavenging gnolls, and hostile outlaws, this fortified rise is the only secure foothold for lawful citizens in the region.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched on high ground in central Westfall, Sentinel Hill stands as a vital sanctuary in an otherwise lawless territory. It features a barracks-style inn, a gryphon roost connecting travelers to Stormwind and beyond, a forge, and a lumber mill, all anchored by the imposing Sentinel Tower. While the surrounding lands have fallen to banditry and ravenous beasts, the encampment maintains a fragile perimeter where travelers, beleaguered farmers, and recruits can regroup under the watchful eyes of veteran defenders.",["t"]="A Bastion in the Dust"},{["b"]="With the royal army detained in Stormwind and unable to spare soldiers to protect outlying territories, Gryan Stoutmantle established the People's Militia directly upon this hill. From here, volunteer fighters organize scouts, coordinate strikes against the Riverpaw gnolls, and investigate the organized banditry tearing through Westfall's abandoned farmsteads. Sentinel Hill is neither an opulent fort nor a comfortable refuge, but a working frontline camp determined to reclaim the kingdom's former breadbasket.",["t"]="Heart of the Militia"}}}}}
t["subzone:sentinel-tower"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,299,24.456.0,27.450.0,35.196.0,42.229.0,34.188.0,40.185.0",["h"]="ddd3a7",["n"]="Torre del Centinela",["s"]="Torre del Centinela. Torre del Centinela corona la cima de la Colina del Centinela, erigiéndose como el principal punto de observación y cuartel general de los defensores en Páramos de Poniente. Desde sus alturas, Gryan Mantorrecio y las Milicias del Pueblo organizan su desesperada defensa contra bandidos, gnolls y la creciente sombra de la Hermandad Defias. Erigida sobre la cresta de la Colina del Centinela, Torre del Centinela es el corazón militar de los inestables Páramos de Poniente. Con el ejército oficial de Ventormenta casi ausente y denegando su ayuda, los voluntarios locales y los veteranos se unieron para crear un reducto central. La torre de piedra otorga a los vigías una vista ininterrumpida de las llanuras polvorientas, desde los campos de calabazas abandonados hasta las brumosas costas, lo que permite dar una alerta temprana cuando los salteadores de caminos renegados o las partidas de saqueo de gnolls comienzan a merodear.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Sentinel Tower represents the grit of ordinary Alliance subjects fighting for their homeland when the high lords in Stormwind have turned a blind eye.",["race:Human"]="For humans of the kingdom, the tower is a painful reminder that the agrarian breadbasket of Stormwind is barely holding together against homegrown rebellion."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Gryan Stoutmantle directs operations from the tower. As head of the People's Militia, he coordinates the defense of Westfall's displaced farmers and manages the recruitment of willing adventurers.",["al"]={"sentinel tower leader","who leads sentinel tower","who runs the tower"},["q"]="Who is in charge at Sentinel Tower?"},{["a"]="It is the only fortified garrison and lookout post left in the central plains. Because Stormwind has left Westfall largely undefended, the tower serves as the last organized bastion of order and safety for refugees in the region.",["al"]={"why sentinel tower matters","purpose of sentinel tower"},["q"]="Why is the tower so important to Westfall?"},{["a"]="You will find militia officers, sentinels keeping watch, quartermasters, and fleeing farmsteader families who have abandoned their ruined lands to seek shelter near its sturdy stone walls.",["al"]={"who is at sentinel tower","sentinel tower occupants"},["q"]="Who stays in and around the tower?"},{["a"]="Sentinels monitor the movements of the Riverpaw gnolls, stray murlocs crawling inland from the coast, and above all, roaming highwaymen and brigands belonging to the Defias Brotherhood.",["al"]={"sentinel tower enemies","what does the tower guard against"},["q"]="What threats are watched from the tower?"}},["kw"]={"defias","gryan stoutmantle","peoples militia","sentinel hill","sentinel tower","watchtower","westfall"},["n"]="Sentinel Tower",["s"]="Sentinel Tower crowns the apex of Sentinel Hill, standing as the primary vantage point and headquarters for defenders in Westfall. From its heights, Gryan Stoutmantle and the People's Militia organize their desperate defense against bandits, gnolls, and the growing shadow of the Defias Brotherhood.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Erected upon the crest of Sentinel Hill, Sentinel Tower is the military heart of unsettled Westfall. With Stormwind's official army largely absent and withholding aid, local volunteers and veterans banded together to create a central redoubt. The stone tower grants lookouts an unbroken view across the dusty plains, from the abandoned pumpkin patches to the misty shores, giving early warning when rogue highwaymen or gnoll raiding parties begin to prowl.",["t"]="Watch over the Wild West"},{["b"]="The tower serves as the command post for Gryan Stoutmantle and the core of the local leadership. Surrounded by makeshift defenses, wounded refugees, and weary soldiers, it operates as both an administrative hub and an emergency shelter for homesteaders driven from their lands. Here, intelligence on the Defias Brotherhood is pieced together, coordinating volunteers into cohesive strikes against the syndicate that has choked the province into ruin.",["t"]="Headquarters of the Militia"}}}}}
t["subzone:sepulcher"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,261,20.549.0,52.153.0,46.254.0,58.231.0,36.178.0",["h"]="ced130",["n"]="El Sepulcro",["s"]="El Sepulcro. El Sepulcro es el principal asentamiento y bastión de los Renegados en Bosque de Argénteos. Antaño un cementerio y cripta funeraria ordinarios de Lordaeron con vistas a la costa occidental, hoy sirve como santuario fortificado para la Horda frente a las amenazas regionales que lo rodean. Encaramado en las colinas sobre la costa de Lordaeron, el Sepulcro fue originalmente un tranquilo cementerio y cripta junto al camino occidental. Tras la Tercera Guerra, los recién emancipados Renegados reutilizaron la antigua bóveda de piedra y sus terrenos como un puesto de avanzada esencial. Rodeado de fuerzas hostiles por todos lados —los huargen salvajes al sur, remanentes errantes de la Plaga al este y magos del Kirin Tor vigilando desde Molino Ámbar—, el Sepulcro proporciona un insólito remanso de seguridad, suministros y mando para los viajeros que recorren Bosque de Argénteos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="For any Horde traveler venturing south from Tirisfal Glades, the Sepulcher offers the only reliable refuge, repair, and flight hub for miles.",["race:Undead"]="The Sepulcher is the staging ground for the Forsaken's struggle to pacify Silverpine Forest, directing operations against lingering Scourge loyalists, Kirin Tor remnants, and feral worgen."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Before the Third War and the fall of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, it was simply a roadside cemetery and stone crypt where local villagers buried their dead.",["al"]={"sepulcher history","what was the sepulcher","who built the sepulcher"},["q"]="What was the Sepulcher before the Forsaken moved in?"},{["a"]="It serves as the Forsaken's sole fortified hub in Silverpine Forest. From this central position, Forsaken scouts and commanders can monitor encroaching Dalaran mages, Scourge holdouts, and the spreading beastly worgen menace lurking near Shadowfang Keep.",["al"]={"why is sepulcher important","forsaken in silverpine","role of the sepulcher"},["q"]="Why is the Sepulcher so vital to the Forsaken?"},{["a"]="Yes. While the base is managed and inhabited entirely by Forsaken deathguards, merchants, and apothecaries, it functions as an official Horde refuge offering respite and trade to orcs, trolls, and tauren passing through the region.",["al"]={"can orcs go to sepulcher","is the sepulcher horde friendly","horde at sepulcher"},["q"]="Are travelers belonging to other Horde races welcome here?"},{["a"]="The settlement is hemmed in by hostile powers: Scourge forces roam to the east, the Kirin Tor holds Ambermill to the southeast, and ferocious worgen stalk the woods to the south.",["al"]={"threats to sepulcher","enemies in silverpine","what attacks sepulcher"},["q"]="What threats surround the Sepulcher?"}},["kw"]={"crypt","deathguard","forsaken outpost","graveyard","sepulcher","silverpine forest","silverpine sepulcher"},["n"]="Sepulcher",["s"]="The Sepulcher is the primary Forsaken settlement and stronghold in Silverpine Forest. Once an ordinary Lordaeron graveyard and burial crypt overlooking the western coast, it now serves as a fortified sanctuary for the Horde against surrounding regional threats.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched in the hills above the Lordaeron coastline, the Sepulcher was originally a quiet cemetery and crypt alongside the western road. In the wake of the Third War, the newly emancipated Forsaken repurposed the ancient stone vault and its grounds into an essential outpost. Surrounded by hostile forces on all sides—the feral worgen to the south, wandering Scourge remnants to the east, and Kirin Tor wizards watching from Ambermill—the Sepulcher provides a rare haven of safety, supplies, and command for travelers marching through Silverpine.",["t"]="A Sanctum in the Fog"}}}}}
t["subzone:shadow-grave"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,244,22.531.0,34.255.0,34.217.0,37.174.0",["h"]="46c116",["n"]="Sepulcro Sombrío",["s"]="Sepulcro Sombrío. Sepulcro Sombrío es una cripta de piedra encaramada en lo alto de los terrenos de enterramiento sobre Camposanto, en Claros de Tirisfal. Sirve como el punto de despertar físico donde los Renegados recién liberados se sacuden el estupor de la muerte y el debilitado control del Rey Exánime. Escondido en las estribaciones rocosas tras las tumbas de Camposanto, el Sepulcro Sombrío es un sencillo mausoleo de piedra con un propósito extraordinario. En sus húmedas bóvedas, los cadáveres levantados para la servidumbre descerebrada de la Plaga despiertan gradualmente al libre albedrío. Bajo la atenta mirada de cuidadores como el Enterrador Mordo, estos no-muertos recién liberados se levantan de sus losas de piedra y dan sus primeros y estremecidos pasos en un mundo que los desprecia, emprendiendo el sendero hacia Camposanto para consagrarse a la Reina Alma en Pena.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Undead"]="Every Forsaken adventurer begins their journey on the cold stone slabs of this crypt, opening their eyes to the grim reality of unlife and free will."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is the crypt where newly awakened Forsaken rise into consciousness. Instead of remaining mindless Scourge thralls in the dirt, these resurrected individuals regain their free will inside the tomb and begin their second life serving Sylvanas Windrunner.",["al"]={"shadow grave purpose","what is shadow grave","shadow grave crypt"},["q"]="What is the Shadow Grave used for?"},{["a"]="Shadow Grave is situated at the top of the hill above the Deathknell Graves, backed against the southern mountains of Tirisfal Glades. A dirt trail winds downhill from its entrance toward the settlement of Deathknell.",["al"]={"where is shadow grave","shadow grave location","shadow grave map"},["q"]="Where is the Shadow Grave located?"},{["a"]="Undertaker Mordo attends the newly awakened within the tomb, assessing whether those rising from the slabs have recovered their minds and are fit to serve the Forsaken cause.",["al"]={"who is in shadow grave","shadow grave npcs","undertaker mordo location"},["q"]="Who oversees the newly awakened here?"}},["kw"]={"awakening","crypt","deathknell","shadow grave","starting tomb","tirisfal glades","undertaker mordo"},["n"]="Shadow Grave",["s"]="Shadow Grave is a stone crypt perched atop the sloping burial grounds above Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. It serves as the physical awakening point where newly liberated Forsaken shake off the stupor of death and the Lich King's faded control.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked into the rocky foothills behind Deathknell Graves, the Shadow Grave is a simple stone mausoleum with an extraordinary purpose. Inside its damp vaults, corpses raised into the mindless servitude of the Scourge gradually awaken to free will. Under the watchful eye of caretakers like Undertaker Mordo, these freshly liberated undead stand up from their stone slabs and take their first shuddering steps into a world that despises them, setting out down the footpath toward Deathknell to pledge themselves to the Banshee Queen.",["t"]="Cradle of the Forsaken"}}}}}
t["subzone:shadowglen"] = {["faq"]={{["a"]="Cañada Umbría es el protegido bosque inicial de los elfos de la noche, ubicado en los confines nororientales de Teldrassil. Es un remanso pacífico y apartado centrado en el imponente árbol Aldrassil, donde los novicios se entrenan bajo la guía de mentores antes de recorrer el Árbol del Mundo.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="1bd6bb",["i"]=1,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="El árbol es Aldrassil, un túmulo arbóreo que constituye el corazón de Cañada Umbría. Su interior hueco sirve como recinto administrativo y núcleo de adiestramiento donde los elfos de la noche novicios conocen a instructores de clase, mentores y cuidadores.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="d4b539",["i"]=2,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="La principal amenaza procede del noroeste, en la Gruta Narácnida, una caverna infestada de arañas venenosas que se deslizan con frecuencia hacia el claro. Los jóvenes defensores tienen la tarea de diezmar a las arañas y calmar a la inquieta fauna local.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="1a17ab",["i"]=3,["q"]="",["sp"]=0},{["a"]="Cañada Umbría está enteramente rodeada de cordilleras salvo por un único sendero hacia el sur. Cruzar este estrecho desfiladero de montaña conduce en dirección sur hacia Aldea Brisa Estelar y el asentamiento de Dolanaar.",["answerOnly"]=true,["h"]="ab4ee0",["i"]=4,["q"]="",["sp"]=0}},["fp"]="10,269,18.533.0,16.444.0,19.264.0,51.216.0,33.239.0,28.197.0",["h"]="74f328",["n"]="Cañada Umbría",["s"]="Cañada Umbría. Cañada Umbría es un valle apartado y en penumbra situado entre las ramas nororientales de Teldrassil. Dominado por el gran túmulo arbóreo de Aldrassil, sirve como refugio seguro donde los jóvenes elfos de la noche dan sus primeros pasos en el servicio antes de aventurarse en el ancho mundo. Resguardada en las copas nororientales de Teldrassil, Cañada Umbría está rodeada por altas crestas que la protegen del resto del mundo. Bañado en un crepúsculo eterno, el valle gira en torno a Aldrassil, un inmenso túmulo arbóreo cuyo tronco hueco alberga a ancianos, sacerdotisas y mentores para los jóvenes elfos de la noche que inician su adiestramiento. La única ruta de salida del valle conduce hacia el sur a través de un estrecho paso de montaña hacia Aldea Brisa Estelar y Dolanaar, lo que convierte a Cañada Umbría en uno de los santuarios más pacíficos y naturalmente fortificados del Árbol del Mundo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Situated high on the boughs of Teldrassil and deep behind guarded ports, Shadowglen stands as one of the Alliance's most insulated and well-defended sanctuary vales.",["race:NightElf"]="Every young night elf begins their active journey here among the sheltered roots of Aldrassil, receiving their first blessings and instructions before facing the perils of Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Shadowglen is the sheltered starting grove for the night elves, located in the northeastern reaches of Teldrassil. It is a peaceful, secluded haven centered around the grand tree Aldrassil, where novices train under mentors before journeying across the World Tree.",["al"]={"what is this place","shadowglen lore","about shadowglen"},["q"]="What is Shadowglen?"},{["a"]="The tree is Aldrassil, a barrow-tree that forms the heart of Shadowglen. Its hollowed interior serves as an administrative lodge and training hub where novice night elves meet class trainers, mentors, and caretakers.",["al"]={"big tree in shadowglen","aldrassil","shadowglen tree"},["q"]="What is the massive tree at the center of the glen?"},{["a"]="The primary threat comes from the northwest in Shadowthread Cave, a cavern infested with venomous spiders that regularly creep out into the glade. Young defenders are tasked with culling the spiders and calming the restless local wildlife.",["al"]={"why are there spiders here","shadowglen dangers","shadowthread cave"},["q"]="What threats exist in Shadowglen?"},{["a"]="Shadowglen is entirely surrounded by ridges except for a single path to the south. Passing through this narrow mountain gap leads southward toward Starbreeze Village and the settlement of Dolanaar.",["al"]={"exit shadowglen","where does the path lead","way out of shadowglen"},["q"]="How do you leave Shadowglen?"}},["kw"]={"aldrassil","kaldorei","night elf starting area","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","teldrassil"},["n"]="Shadowglen",["s"]="Shadowglen is a secluded, twilit vale nestled within the northeastern boughs of Teldrassil. Dominated by the great barrow-tree Aldrassil, it serves as the safe haven where young night elves take their first steps into service before journeying out into the wider world.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the northeastern canopy of Teldrassil, Shadowglen is ringed by high ridges that shelter it from the rest of the world. Bathed in eternal dusk, the vale centers on Aldrassil, a massive barrow-tree whose hollowed trunk houses elders, priestesses, and mentors for young night elves beginning their training. The only route out of the valley leads south through a narrow mountain pass toward Starbreeze Village and Dolanaar, making Shadowglen one of the most naturally fortified and peaceful sanctuaries on the World Tree.",["t"]="A Sheltered Cradle"},{["b"]="Despite its tranquil seclusion, Shadowglen is not entirely free from danger. In the extreme northwest lies Shadowthread Cave, a dark cavern infested with venomous spiders that constantly threaten the tranquil glade. Even on the pristine branches of Teldrassil, vigilance is required, and fledgling defenders are tasked with driving back the encroaching vermin and untamed wildlife before venturing into the broader expanse of the boughs beyond.",["t"]="Creeping Shadows"}}}}}
t["subzone:shadowthread-cave"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,263,24.490.0,17.400.0,35.151.0,46.192.0,25.200.0,48.183.0",["h"]="ae0e24",["n"]="Gruta Narácnida",["s"]="Gruta Narácnida. La Gruta Narácnida es una caverna húmeda excavada en los riscos del noroeste de Cañada Umbría, en Teldrassil. Habitada tradicionalmente por arañas Tejerrabiza autóctonas, la cueva se ha vuelto recientemente y de forma peligrosa agresiva bajo el dominio de su matriarca, Githyiss la Vil. Escondida en el perímetro sombrío de Cañada Umbría, la Gruta Narácnida ha servido durante mucho tiempo como guarida natural para las arañas gigantes de Teldrassil. En años anteriores, estos arácnidos coexistían pacíficamente junto a las ramas nacientes del Árbol del Mundo. Sin embargo, recientemente su temperamento se ha vuelto ferozmente territorial. Gruesas capas de seda de Tejerrabiza obstruyen ahora los pasillos de piedra, y la naturaleza agresiva de la prole supone un peligro inmediato para los jóvenes kaldorei que dan sus primeros pasos más allá de Aldrassil.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The unchecked aggression of the Webwood brood in Shadowthread Cave is a troubling indicator to druids that the natural harmony of Teldrassil is deeply disturbed.",["race:NightElf"]="For young night elves, clearing Shadowthread Cave and slaying Githyiss the Vile serves as one of their very first trials in defending their sacred home from creeping corruption."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Shadowthread Cave lies in the northwest corner of Shadowglen, nestled against the rocky hillside bordering the night elf starting valley in Teldrassil.",["al"]={"shadowthread cave location","where is shadowthread cave","find shadowthread cave"},["q"]="Where is Shadowthread Cave located?"},{["a"]="While spiders have always dwelled within the cave, a foul sickness and growing imbalance across Teldrassil has driven the local wildlife mad, turning the webwood spiders exceptionally violent.",["al"]={"why are spiders hostile","spider corruption shadowthread","why spiders attacking"},["q"]="Why are the spiders in the cave so aggressive?"},{["a"]="Githyiss the Vile is a massive, venomous webwood spider matriarch nestled at the deepest point of Shadowthread Cave. She is the mother of the aggressive brood threatening young kaldorei in Shadowglen.",["al"]={"githyiss","who is githyiss","shadowthread spider boss"},["q"]="Who is Githyiss the Vile?"},{["a"]="The cave is packed with layers of dense, naturally spun webwood silk, a valuable and resilient crafting material woven by the endless swarms of arachnids inhabiting its dark chambers.",["al"]={"shadowthread silk","spider silk shadowglen"},["q"]="What makes the cave valuable despite the danger?"}},["kw"]={"githyiss the vile","shadowglen","shadowthread cave","spider silk","teldrassil","webwood spider"},["n"]="Shadowthread Cave",["s"]="Shadowthread Cave is a damp cavern carved into the northwest cliffs of Shadowglen on Teldrassil. Traditionally inhabited by indigenous Webwood spiders, the cave has recently turned dangerously aggressive under the dominion of their broodmother, Githyiss the Vile.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the shaded perimeter of Shadowglen, Shadowthread Cave has long served as a natural lair for Teldrassil's giant spiders. In earlier years, these arachnids coexisted quietly alongside the nascent boughs of the World Tree. Recently, however, their temperament has turned fiercely territorial. Thick layers of webwood silk now choke the stone corridors, and the aggressive nature of the brood poses an immediate hazard to young kaldorei taking their first steps beyond Aldrassil.",["t"]="A Brood Growing Restless"},{["b"]="The primary menace lurking deep within the cave's darkest recesses is Githyiss the Vile, a monstrous broodmother whose ferocity far outstrips the common webwood crawlers. Novice night elf sentinels and druids are dispatched to the cave to curb the spider infestation and slay Githyiss, ensuring that the corruption touching Teldrassil's wildlife does not overrun the sanctuary of Shadowglen entirely.",["t"]="Githyiss the Vile"}}}}}
t["subzone:shimmer-ridge"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,282,22.510.0,24.439.0,31.140.0,27.168.0,47.205.0,54.202.0",["h"]="382d71",["n"]="Monte Luz",["s"]="Monte Luz. Monte Luz es una escarpada meseta situada en el norte de Dun Morogh, justo al oeste de las Puertas de Forjaz. Ocupadas por los hostiles troles Frostmane, las alturas rocosas constan de dos campamentos unidos por un destartalado puente y son famosas por ser el único lugar donde se recolecta la potente hierba centelleante cardaluz. Encaramado a lo largo de las escarpadas laderas justo al oeste de la imponente entrada de Forjaz, Monte Luz sirve como un reducto activo para la tribu de troles Frostmane. Dividido en dos campamentos gemelos a ambos lados de un abismo y unidos por una pasarela de madera, el enclave está fuertemente custodiado por troles carroñeros y sus jabalíes de montaña amaestrados. Su proximidad al camino principal y a la capital de los enanos supone una molestia constante para los viajeros y las patrullas de las montañas, que deben permanecer continuamente en guardia contra las incursiones oportunistas desde las alturas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Herbalism"]="While ordinary flora struggles in Dun Morogh's sub-zero climate, Shimmer Ridge uniquely supports valuable shimmerweed baskets tended among the Frostmane camps.",["race:Dwarf"]="Nestled in the shadow of Ironforge's gates, Shimmer Ridge is an irritating reminder of the persistent Frostmane threat and the dangerous source of choice shimmerweed for legendary dwarven stout."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Shimmer Ridge is situated in northern Dun Morogh, directly to the west of the massive Gates of Ironforge that lead into the dwarven capital.",["al"]={"shimmer ridge location","where is shimmer ridge","find shimmer ridge"},["q"]="Where is Shimmer Ridge located?"},{["a"]="The ridge is occupied by the indigenous Frostmane troll tribe, who have established dual camps connected by a bridge and defend the heights alongside their tamed boars.",["al"]={"who lives at shimmer ridge","shimmer ridge enemies","trolls at shimmer ridge"},["q"]="Who controls Shimmer Ridge?"},{["a"]="Shimmerweed is a distinct mountain herb that thrives on the cold slopes of the ridge. Local dwarven brewers value it immensely as an essential ingredient for specialized, flavorful recipes of highland ale.",["al"]={"shimmerweed use","what is shimmerweed","shimmer weed purpose"},["q"]="What is shimmerweed and why is it sought after?"},{["a"]="Ironforge's military is occupied with broader defense and external matters, leaving local threats like the Frostmane enclaves in Dun Morogh to be managed by regional mountaineers and wandering recruits.",["al"]={"why ironforge ignores shimmer ridge","ironforge vs frostmane","dwarf response shimmer ridge"},["q"]="Why don't the dwarves clear out the trolls completely?"}},["kw"]={"dun morogh","frostmane","ironforge","mountaineers","shimmer ridge","shimmerweed","trolls"},["n"]="Shimmer Ridge",["s"]="Shimmer Ridge is a rugged highland nestled in northern Dun Morogh, directly west of the Gates of Ironforge. Occupied by hostile Frostmane trolls, the rocky heights consist of two camps joined by a rickety bridge and are renowned as the sole harvesting ground for potent shimmerweed.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched along the craggy slopes just west of Ironforge's mighty entryway, Shimmer Ridge serves as an active redoubt for the Frostmane troll tribe. Divided into twin camps straddling a chasm and linked by a wooden span, the enclave is heavily guarded by troll scavengers and their tamed mountain boars. Their proximity to the main roadway and the dwarven capital poses a continuous nuisance to travelers and mountain patrols, who must constantly remain on guard against opportunistic raids from the high ground.",["t"]="A Frostmane Stronghold"},{["b"]="Aside from strategic positioning, the ridge is famous for cultivating shimmerweed, a plant grown by the Frostmane trolls. Prized by local dwarven brewmasters for crafting potent, flavorful highland ales, the herb cannot easily be gathered elsewhere. Daring mountaineers and young recruits frequently risk Frostmane ambushes and savage tusked beasts simply to harvest fresh baskets of the precious botanical directly from the trolls' plots.",["t"]="The Price of Shimmerweed"}}}}}
t["subzone:shimmering-flats"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,303,23.588.0,19.504.0,59.255.0,41.336.0,51.298.0,54.164.0",["h"]="8be5b5",["n"]="El Desierto de Sal",["s"]="El Desierto de Sal. El Desierto de Sal es una extensa llanura salina situada en el extremo suroriental de Las Mil Agujas, en la frontera con el desierto de Tanaris. Antaño el lecho de un antiguo lago, esta extensión abrasada por el sol es ahora célebre por las rivalidades mecánicas a alta velocidad del Circuito del Espejismo y por una dura fauna de bestias del desierto. Extendiéndose bajo el cegador sol del sur, El Desierto de Sal es el vasto lecho de un lago seco desprovisto de vegetación, salpicado de huesos de tortuga blanqueados por el sol e incluso del pecio de madera de un antiguo navío de vela. Su superficie completamente llana y continua lo convierte en el principal campo de pruebas de Kalimdor para vehículos experimentales. En el centro de la llanura se encuentra el Circuito del Espejismo, donde manitas gnomos y goblins se enfrentan constantemente para ver qué bólidos cohete, girocópteros y motores alcanzan las mayores velocidades, lo que a menudo resulta en ardientes colisiones y humeantes cráteres por toda la corteza blanca.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="The salt flats are a pilgrimage site for engineers, littered with scrap, fuel experiments, and high-speed vehicular trial runs fueled by the endless rivalry between goblin and gnomish machinists.",["race:Gnome"]="Out on the Mirage Raceway, gnomish pilots and mechanostriders boldly defend gnomish engineering pride against the volatile, explosive designs of their goblin rivals."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Shimmering Flats was once a massive inland lake that dried up long ago. The wrecked vessel resting in the northern stretch of the flats is a remnant of that ancient body of water, left behind when the lake evaporated into the vast salt pan seen today.",["al"]={"ship in shimmering flats","boat in salt flats","wrecked boat thousand needles"},["q"]="Why is there a ruined ship out in the middle of the desert?"},{["a"]="The unbroken, flat salt crust provides the perfect terrain for testing rocket cars and cutting-edge mechanical contraptions. Rather than fighting over territory, local gnomes and goblins established the Mirage Raceway to fuel their technological rivalry, endlessly trying to outdo each other in speed, engineering, and reckless bravado.",["al"]={"raceway lore","why are they racing","gnomes and goblins salt flats"},["q"]="Why are gnomes and goblins here together?"},{["a"]="The Rustmaul Dig Site was established by dwarven archaeologists, who were soon attacked by a Horde raiding party led by Moktar Krin. Then the diggers inadvertently broke into a subterranean silithid hive, releasing swarms of insectoid horrors that drove everyone out and overran the southern flats.",["al"]={"rustmaul dig site lore","what happened to rustmaul","bugs in salt flats"},["q"]="What happened to the dwarven dig site in the south?"},{["a"]="Following the tracks southeast across the salt pan leads directly to the mountain pass that opens into the vast desert of Tanaris and the neutral port of Gadgetzan.",["al"]={"where does shimmering flats go","how to get to tanaris","exit to tanaris"},["q"]="Where does the road through the Shimmering Flats lead?"}},["kw"]={"mirage raceway","pozzik","rustmaul","salt flats","shimmering flats","silithid","tanaris","thousand needles"},["n"]="Shimmering Flats",["s"]="The Shimmering Flats is an expansive salt flat lying at the southeastern tip of Thousand Needles, bordering the desert of Tanaris. Once the bed of an ancient lake, this sun-baked expanse is now famous for the high-speed mechanical rivalries of the Mirage Raceway and a harsh population of desert beasts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stretching out under the blinding southern sun, the Shimmering Flats is a vast dried lakebed devoid of vegetation, dotted with the sun-bleached bones of turtles and even the wooden wreck of an ancient sailing vessel. Its sheer, unbroken level surface makes it the premier testing ground on Kalimdor for experimental vehicles. At the center of the flats lies the Mirage Raceway, where gnome and goblin tinkerers constantly clash to see whose rocket cars, gyrocopters, and engines can achieve the highest speeds—often resulting in fiery crashes and smoking craters across the white crust.",["t"]="A Bed of Salt and Speed"},{["b"]="Beyond the roaring engines of the raceway, the basin is far from peaceful. Hardened basilisks, aggressive scorpids, and circling vultures prey upon anything that slows down on the open expanse. Further south, the ground grows treacherous around the Rustmaul Dig Site. Originally excavated by dwarven prospectors before being contested by the Horde, the quarry was entirely abandoned when picks cracked into subterranean tunnels, unleashing a swarm of vicious silithid into the southern edge of the flats.",["t"]="Hazards of the Salt"}}}}}
t["subzone:shining-strand"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,349,21.638.0,18.433.1,36.238.0,48.285.0,60.241.0,31.175.0",["h"]="0e11c5",["n"]="La Playa Plateada",["s"]="La Playa Plateada. La Playa Plateada es la franja de costa que bordea el Lago Lordamere a lo largo del este del Bosque de Argénteos, extendiéndose hacia el sur desde las Ruinas de Lordaeron hacia las escarpadas estribaciones de Alterac. Antaño dominadas por los agresivos múrlocs Vile Fin, las costas son ahora un terreno disputado donde los campamentos de los Renegados vigilan el agua y se enfrentan a los huargen invasores. A lo largo del borde oriental del Bosque de Argénteos, La Playa Plateada bordea las brumosas aguas del Lago Lordamere. En tiempos anteriores, la tribu de múrlocs Vile Fin estableció varios asentamientos agresivos a lo largo de estos bajíos, lo que suponía un peligro mortal para cualquiera que intentara recorrer el camino del lago. Aunque los Vile Fin han desplazado en gran medida su presencia hacia el este, a las Islas del Alba, la costa dista mucho de ser pacífica. Los exploradores y boticarios de los Renegados han establecido posiciones a lo largo de la playa, enfrentándose a los huargen ferales que surgen de la espesura del bosque y manteniendo un ojo vigilante tanto en las aguas como en las colinas que limitan con Alterac.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="The strand offers a clear, if perilous, transit corridor along Lordamere Lake connecting the northern approaches of Silverpine to the passages heading toward the Alterac Mountains.",["race:Undead"]="Holding the Shining Strand protects the Undercity's southern lake flank and provides valuable specimens for the Royal Apothecary Society's research into a new plague."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Shining Strand is the eastern shoreline of Silverpine Forest, bordering the waters of Lordamere Lake. It begins just south of the Ruins of Lordaeron and ends against the rough hills that separate Silverpine from the Alterac Mountains.",["al"]={"shining strand location","where is shining strand","silverpine coast"},["q"]="Where is the Shining Strand located?"},{["a"]="Forsaken encampments along the strand contend regularly with prowling worgen that emerge from the Silverpine woods. While the Vile Fin murlocs previously held strongpoints on the shore, most have relocated to the nearby Dawning Isles, though aquatic threats still lurk in the shallows.",["al"]={"shining strand monsters","what is on shining strand","shining strand enemies"},["q"]="What threats are found along the Shining Strand?"},{["a"]="The late Apothecary Berard documented that the native Vile Fin murlocs carried hardened tumors with unique physiological traits. The Society saw these growths as promising ingredients in their ongoing research to develop a lethal new plague.",["al"]={"apothecary berard","shining strand plague","new plague tumor"},["q"]="Why is the Royal Apothecary Society interested in this area?"},{["a"]="After pressure from Forsaken forces securing the shoreline, the Vile Fin tribe relocated their major encampments off the mainland coast to the Dawning Isles in Lordamere Lake.",["al"]={"where are murlocs silverpine","vile fin location","shining strand murlocs"},["q"]="Where did the local murlocs go?"}},["kw"]={"apothecary berard","dawning isles","lordamere lake","shining strand","silverpine forest","vile fin","worgen"},["n"]="Shining Strand",["s"]="The Shining Strand is the strip of shoreline hugging Lordamere Lake along eastern Silverpine Forest, stretching south from the Ruins of Lordaeron toward the rugged foothills of Alterac. Once dominated by aggressive Vile Fin murlocs, the shores are now contested ground where Forsaken encampments watch the water and skirmish with encroaching worgen.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Running along the eastern edge of Silverpine Forest, the Shining Strand borders the misty waters of Lordamere Lake. In earlier days, the Vile Fin tribe of murlocs established several aggressive settlements along these shallows, posing a deadly hazard to anyone attempting to travel the lake road. While the Vile Fins have largely shifted their presence eastward to the Dawning Isles, the shore remains far from peaceful. Forsaken scouts and apothecaries have established footholds along the strand, contending with feral worgen roaming out from the deep woods and keeping a watchful eye on both the waters and the hills bordering Alterac.",["t"]="A Contested Coastline"},{["b"]="Beyond its strategic position between Lordaeron and the southern borders, the Shining Strand and its neighboring waters drew early attention from the Royal Apothecary Society. The late Apothecary Berard recorded notes on unusual hardened tumors harvested from the local Vile Fin murlocs, theorizing that their corrupted anatomy could serve as a valuable catalyst in concocting a new plague for Sylvanas Windrunner's fledgling nation.",["t"]="Alchemical Harvest"}}}}}
t["subzone:shrine-of-the-dormant-flame"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="27,297,27.723.0,49.218.0,39.242.0,19.211.0,41.245.0",["h"]="12e9dc",["n"]="Santuario de la Llama Latente",["s"]="Santuario de la Llama Latente. Encaramado en la cima del pico más alto al noroeste del Valle de los Retos, el Santuario de la Llama Latente es un refugio apartado y venerado por los chamanes de la Horda. Guiados por su solitario guardián, Telf Joolam, los iniciados emprenden la peligrosa ascensión para entrar en comunión con el elemento del fuego y demostrar su maestría espiritual. Llegar al Santuario de la Llama Latente requiere enfrentarse a un sendero estrecho y serpenteante que comienza junto al Río Furia del Sur, en el extremo suroeste de Southfury Watershed. Muy por encima de los riscos rojos de Durotar, la cumbre de la montaña ofrece una vista imponente de las tierras circundantes, aunque un solo paso en falso por el precipicio supone una muerte segura. En este tranquilo refugio deambula Telf Joolam, un ermitaño solitario encargado de supervisar los ritos sagrados. Para los aspirantes a chamán orcos y trols que emprenden el ritual de La llamada del Fuego, el brasero del santuario sirve como crisol donde deben prender los carbones dormidos usando el rescoldo de un elemental derrotado, demostrando su poder para comunicarse con los destructivos espíritus de la llama y respetarlos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="Every young orc and troll shaman must make the arduous trek up this crag to kindle their spiritual connection with fire and earn their Fire Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="Tucked away in the mountains above Durotar, this isolated shrine preserves ancient elemental rites vital to the spiritual heart of the new Horde."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The path begins along the Southfury River on the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed, just northwest of the Valley of Trials. A narrow mountain trail spirals around the peak, leading directly up to the summit.",["al"]={"how to get to shrine of the dormant flame","path to dormant flame","climb dormant flame mountain"},["q"]="How do you reach the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?"},{["a"]="The shrine is a sacred site where aspiring Horde shaman learn to understand and command the element of fire. As part of their Call of Fire journey, initiates must travel to this summit to prepare a ritual draft and kindle the dormant brazier.",["al"]={"shrine of dormant flame purpose","why do shaman go here","call of fire shrine"},["q"]="Why is this shrine important to shaman?"},{["a"]="Telf Joolam is a solitary troll hermit who serves as the keeper of the shrine. He guides young shaman through their trials, concocting a draught of fire to awaken their spiritual sight and testing their resolve.",["al"]={"who is telf joolam","dormant flame npc","shrine keeper"},["q"]="Who is Telf Joolam?"},{["a"]="Shaman who have gathered the required ritual components and defeated a hostile fire elemental place its burning ember into the brazier. This acts as an offering to prove they have the strength and discipline to tame the volatile spirit of flame.",["al"]={"brazier of dormant flame","igniting the flame","shrine brazier quest"},["q"]="What happens when you kindle the brazier?"}},["kw"]={"call of fire","dormant flame","durotar","fire totem","shrine","southfury watershed","telf joolam","valley of trials"},["n"]="Shrine of the Dormant Flame",["s"]="Perched atop the highest peak northwest of the Valley of Trials, the Shrine of the Dormant Flame is a secluded sanctuary revered by Horde shaman. Guided by its solitary keeper, Telf Joolam, initiates make the treacherous climb to commune with the element of fire and prove their spiritual mastery.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Reaching the Shrine of the Dormant Flame requires braving a narrow, winding trail that begins along the Southfury River at the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed. High above the red cliffs of Durotar, the mountain summit offers a commanding view of the surrounding lands, though a single misstep along the precipice means certain death. In this quiet refuge wanders Telf Joolam, a solitary hermit tasked with overseeing sacred rites. For aspiring orc and troll shaman undertaking the ritual Call of Fire, the shrine's brazier serves as the crucible where they must ignite slumbering coals using the ember of a vanquished elemental, proving their power to commune with and respect the destructive spirits of flame.",["t"]="A Summit of Trial and Flame"}}}}}
t["subzone:shrine-of-the-fallen-warrior"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="28,327,14.608.0,27.487.0,50.210.0,37.199.0,46.121.0,52.209.0,49.162.0",["h"]="96f9b3",["n"]="Santuario del Guerrero Caído",["s"]="Santuario del Guerrero Caído. Encaramado en una cresta apartada al oeste de El Cruce se encuentra el Santuario del Guerrero Caído, un tranquilo monumento conmemorativo que domina las extensas sabanas rojas de Los Baldíos. Marcado por un plinto de piedra con las iniciales «MK» grabadas y el cuerpo de un guerrero orco caído, está custodiado por la apacible presencia de un Ángel de la Resurrección llamado Koiter. Escondido en lo alto de las colinas al noroeste de El Cruce, el Santuario del Guerrero Caído se alza como un remanso inusualmente solemne en medio del polvo y el peligro de Los Baldíos. Para encontrarlo, los viajeros deben subir por un sendero sinuoso por la cresta al suroeste de la cima hasta alcanzar un suave montículo. En la cima descansa un monumento de piedra tallada, con las iniciales «MK» grabadas en su plinto. Ante él yace la figura en armadura de un guerrero orco en reposo, vigilado día y noche por un Ángel de la Resurrección con nombre propio: Koiter. Aquí no suenan cuernos de batalla, solo reina una tranquila contemplación en honor a un campeón que recorrió las tierras de Kalimdor.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Warrior"]="Warriors of all races often make a quiet pilgrimage to this hill, paying respects to a fallen brother-in-arms who fought bravely before passing into legend.",["faction:Horde"]="Set right in the heartland of Horde territory, this solitary resting place captures the honor, duty, and sacrifice at the core of the shamanic and warrior traditions of Kalimdor."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The shrine sits atop a hill west of the Crossroads in the northern Barrens. Travelers can reach it by locating the base of a ridge southwest of the elevation and following a winding path up to the grassy knoll.",["al"]={"shrine location","where is the shrine","how to get to shrine of fallen warrior"},["q"]="Where is the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior located?"},{["a"]="In-game, he represents a revered fallen warrior. In reality, he is modeled directly after Twincruiser, the orc warrior character played by late Blizzard artist Michel Koiter during early development.",["al"]={"who is the dead orc","fallen warrior identity","twincruiser"},["q"]="Who is the orc lying upon the plinth?"},{["a"]="The runic initials 'MK' honor Michel Koiter, a senior artist who passed away in 2004 during the development of the world.",["al"]={"mk initials","what does mk stand for","letters on the stone"},["q"]="What does the 'MK' carved into the stone mean?"},{["a"]="The Spirit Healer is named Koiter. Unlike ordinary Spirit Healers that only appear to spirits walking in death, Koiter stands in vigil and can be seen clearly by living wanderers who make the trek up the hill.",["al"]={"spirit healer koiter","angel at the shrine","who is the ghost"},["q"]="Who is the Spirit Healer standing beside the shrine?"},{["a"]="No. The Shrine of the Fallen Warrior is not part of any questline or faction conflict. It exists purely as a solemn place of reflection, remembrance, and tribute.",["al"]={"shrine quest","quest for fallen warrior","is there a quest here"},["q"]="Are there any quests associated with this shrine?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","crossroads","koiter","memorial","michel koiter","shrine of the fallen warrior","twincruiser"},["n"]="Shrine of the Fallen Warrior",["s"]="Perched upon a secluded ridge west of the Crossroads lies the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior, a quiet memorial overlooking the sweeping red savannahs of the Barrens. Marked by a stone plinth bearing the initials 'MK' and the body of a fallen orc warrior, it is watched over by the gentle presence of a Spirit Healer named Koiter.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away high upon the hills northwest of the Crossroads, the Shrine of the Fallen Warrior stands as an unusually solemn haven amidst the dust and peril of the Barrens. To find it, travelers must scale a winding ridge pathway southwest of the summit until they reach a gentle mound. Upon the summit rests a carved stone monument, its plinth carved with the initials 'MK'. Before it lies the armored form of an orc warrior at rest, watched over day and night by a named Spirit Healer known as Koiter. There are no battle horns here, only quiet contemplation honoring a champion who walked Kalimdor's lands.",["t"]="A Silent Vigil"},{["b"]="Within the world, the shrine stands as an enduring tribute to a departed champion of the Horde whose soul lingers in the care of the spirits. Outside the realm, the monument serves as a heartfelt tribute created by the game's artists to honor Michel Koiter, a beloved illustrator who passed away during the development of the world. The resting warrior is modeled precisely after Koiter's own beta character, Twincruiser, immortalizing his presence forever beneath Kalimdor's open skies.",["t"]="The Meaning of the Memorial"}}}}}
t["subzone:si-7-stormwind-city"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="21,345,32.604.0,29.438.1,13.159.0,28.175.0,43.127.0,38.297.0",["h"]="a3b602",["n"]="IV:7 (Ciudad de Ventormenta)",["s"]="IV:7 (Ciudad de Ventormenta). Escondida en la esquina oriental del Casco Antiguo, esta modesta mansión de piedra alberga el cuartel general de Inteligencia de Ventormenta, Sección 7 (IV:7), el servicio de élite de espionaje e inteligencia del reino de Ventormenta. Tras sus pesadas puertas, el maestro de espías Mathias Shaw y sus agentes de mayor rango vigilan discretamente las amenazas al reino, coordinando operativos encubiertos por todo el territorio. Para el transeúnte ocasional en el Casco Antiguo, esta estructura de piedra fortificada apenas se diferencia de una mansión común o de un cuartel militar. En realidad, sirve como centro neurálgico para Inteligencia de Ventormenta, Sección 7. Dirigida por el Maestro Mathias Shaw, IV:7 recopila información, realiza labores de vigilancia y ejecuta operaciones encubiertas para proteger al reino de la subversión. Mientras la guardia de la ciudad patrulla los adoquines y la Guardia Real defiende Plaza del Rey, IV:7 trabaja en los márgenes, entrenando instructores y enviando operativos sigilosos contra enemigos extranjeros, saboteadores y disturbios internos por igual.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="For Alliance rogues, the SI:7 building is a vital professional hub offering advanced class training, poison supplies, and clandestine assignments direct from Spymaster Mathias Shaw.",["faction:Alliance"]="As the unseen foundation of Stormwind's defense, SI:7's intelligence network provides the Alliance military with crucial reconnaissance against threats to the throne."},["faq"]={{["a"]="SI:7 stands for Stormwind Intelligence, Section 7. It is the premier covert espionage, reconnaissance, and assassination agency serving the Crown of Stormwind.",["al"]={"what is si7","who are si:7","si 7 meaning"},["q"]="What is SI:7?"},{["a"]="Master Mathias Shaw leads the organization from within the building. Mathias oversees all field assignments, intelligence networks, and strategic reconnaissance for the crown.",["al"]={"who is the leader of si7","si7 boss","who runs si:7"},["q"]="Who leads SI:7 in Stormwind?"},{["a"]="The headquarters is situated in Old Town, tucked along the southeastern edge of the district near the canal and training yards.",["al"]={"where is si7","si7 location","how to get to si7"},["q"]="Where in the city is this building located?"},{["a"]="SI:7 tracks subversive activities throughout Stormwind's territories, and the Defias Brotherhood represents the most dangerous insurrection within the realm. Shaw's operatives have placed undercover agents and scouts throughout Westfall to pinpoint their leadership and disrupt their supply lines.",["al"]={"defias brotherhood si7","why is si7 watching defias"},["q"]="Why is SI:7 so interested in Westfall?"}},["kw"]={"barracks","defias","espionage","mathias shaw","old town","rogues","si7","si:7","spymaster","stormwind"},["n"]="SI:7 (Stormwind City)",["s"]="Tucked away in the eastern corner of Old Town, this unassuming stone manor houses the headquarters of SI:7, the kingdom of Stormwind's elite intelligence and espionage service. Behind its heavy doors, spymaster Master Mathias Shaw and his senior operatives quietly monitor threats to the realm, coordinating undercover agents across the kingdom.",["sec"]={{["b"]="To the casual passerby in Old Town, this fortified stone structure looks little different from a standard manor or military barracks. In truth, it serves as the nerve center for Stormwind Intelligence, Section 7. Directed by Master Mathias Shaw, SI:7 gathers intelligence, conducts surveillance, and executes covert operations to protect the kingdom from subversion. While the city guard patrols the open cobblestones and the Royal Guard defends King's Square, SI:7 works in the margins, training handlers and dispatching stealthy operatives against foreign enemies, saboteurs, and domestic unrest alike.",["t"]="Heart of the Kingdom's Espionage"},{["b"]="With King Varian Wrynn mysteriously missing and the Defias Brotherhood spreading chaos through Westfall and Duskwood, the headquarters hums with constant covert activity. Intelligence reports funnel into the building from deep-cover scouts across human lands. Down in the cellars and weapon-lined training rooms, lethal techniques are refined and missions assigned to counter threats long before they can reach the boy-king's throne room.",["t"]="A Watchful Eye on the Shadows"}}}}}
t["subzone:silver-stream-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,394,31.556.0,20.490.0,52.233.0,32.202.0,42.169.0,46.195.0",["h"]="77d891",["n"]="Mina de Fuenteplata",["s"]="Mina de Fuenteplata. La Mina de Fuenteplata es una mina enana agotada situada en el norte de Loch Modan, resguardada entre la Estación de Algaz y la Presa de las Tres Cabezas. Antaño una rica veta de plata para el reino de Forjaz, el hueco excavado se reconvirtió en un depósito de suministros de la Liga de Mineros antes de ser invadido por alimañas. Hoy en día, los kóbolds Rata de Túnel ocupan los túneles, acumulando equipo robado y raras curiosidades minerales. La Mina de Fuenteplata rebosaba antaño de valioso mineral y contribuyó en gran medida a las reservas de plata de Forjaz. Con el tiempo, los picos de los enanos excavaron lo suficiente como para agotar las vetas principales, convirtiendo las extensas cámaras en un complejo subterráneo vacío. En lugar de abandonar las laboriosas obras de tierra, la Liga de Mineros transformó los pozos en un depósito de almacenamiento seguro para herramientas, cajas de minería y equipo regional. También sirve como la única fuente conocida de las raras Charged Rift Gems, que atraen a arcanistas inquisitivos en busca de delicados componentes de sastrería.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Apprentice mages journey into the dangerous kobold-infested tunnels specifically to extract Charged Rift Gems, an indispensable ingredient for crafting ritual garments.",["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves, Silver Stream Mine is an infuriating loss of hard-earned infrastructure, where clumsy kobolds now sully a respectable Ironforge Miners' League depot."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Originally, it was a productive silver mine excavated by the dwarves of Ironforge. After the veins ran dry, the Ironforge Miners' League repurposed the vacant subterranean halls into a storage depot for tools and excavation supplies.",["al"]={"what is silver stream mine","silver stream history","why was silver stream built"},["q"]="What was the Silver Stream Mine originally used for?"},{["a"]="The mine has been completely overrun by Tunnel Rat kobolds. They chased off the dwarf caretakers and now guard the tunnels, hoarding the League's abandoned supply crates and digging for residual scraps.",["al"]={"who lives in silver stream mine","silver stream mobs","what is inside silver stream mine"},["q"]="Who currently occupies the mine?"},{["a"]="The mine is the only known source of Charged Rift Gems. These volatile, magically reactive stones are sought after by Alliance arcanists to weave potent enchanted robes.",["al"]={"mage quest silver stream","charged rift gems","silver stream mage robes"},["q"]="Why do mages travel to Silver Stream Mine?"},{["a"]="Behind the mine sit broken orcish wagons and ruined catapults, weathered remnants of earlier wartime conflicts that threatened the passages connecting Loch Modan and the northern mountain passes.",["al"]={"orc wagons behind silver stream","broken catapults loch modan mine","horde siege engines loch modan"},["q"]="What are the ruined catapults behind the mine?"}},["kw"]={"charged rift gem","kobold","loch modan","miners league","silver stream mine","tunnel rat"},["n"]="Silver Stream Mine",["s"]="Silver Stream Mine is a depleted dwarf mine located in northern Loch Modan, nestled between Algaz Station and the Stonewrought Dam. Once a rich silver vein for the kingdom of Ironforge, the excavated hollow was repurposed as a Miners' League supply depot before being overrun by vermin. Today, Tunnel Rat kobolds squat inside the tunnels, hoarding stolen equipment and rare mineral curiosities.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Silver Stream Mine once flowed with precious ore, contributing heavily to the silver reserves of Ironforge. In time, the dwarf pickaxes dug deep enough to exhaust the primary veins, turning the sprawling chambers into an empty subterranean complex. Rather than abandon the hard-won earthworks, the Miners' League transformed the shafts into a secure storage depot for tools, mining crates, and regional equipment. It also serves as the only known source of rare Charged Rift Gems, which draw inquisitive arcanists searching for delicate tailoring reagents.",["t"]="From Rich Vein to Storage Depot"},{["b"]="The quiet depot did not remain secure for long. Aggressive Tunnel Rat kobolds, drawn by the smell of unattended tools, candle wax, and forgotten subterranean crevices, swarmed the shafts in large numbers. The Miners' League caretakers were promptly driven out into the Loch Modan cold. Now, the kobolds guard the stolen dwarf crates with manic fervor, while old, shattered orcish catapults and wagons rest forgotten outside the rear entrances, silent reminders of older frontier skirmishes.",["t"]="The Kobold Incursion"}}}}}
t["subzone:silverwind-refuge"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,253,18.477.0,31.191.0,35.107.0,38.147.0",["h"]="1cacba",["n"]="Refugio Brisa de Plata",["s"]="Refugio Brisa de Plata. El Refugio Brisa de Plata es un sereno asentamiento de los elfos de la noche situado en el centro-sur de Vallefresno, justo al norte del Lago Mystral. Protegido por centinelas y elementales de agua aliados, ofrece un acogedor refugio para los viajeros que recorren los senderos boscosos de la espesura. Ubicado entre las plácidas aguas del Lago Mystral y el Lago Iris al norte, el Refugio Brisa de Plata se erige como una de las principales paradas de postas de los elfos de la noche en el centro de Vallefresno, junto a Astranaar. Cuenta con una cómoda posada, artesanos y maestros de profesión que instruyen a los viajeros en herboristería, alquimia, desuello y caza. Custodiado por firmes centinelas junto a espíritus de agua locales, el retiro sirve como un pacífico lugar de descanso para los aliados que atraviesan los umbríos bosques ancestrales.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance wanderers traversing Ashenvale, Silverwind Refuge provides a reliable camp to rest, restock supplies, and refine wilderness trades without venturing all the way to Astranaar.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The refuge serves as a vital stop in Ashenvale for gatherers, offering on-site herbalism training surrounded by the rich flora of Mystral Lake."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Silverwind Refuge is an Alliance settlement, built and maintained by the night elves. It is heavily guarded by the Sentinels, alongside water elementals who help protect the tranquil grounds.",["al"]={"who owns silverwind refuge","is silverwind alliance or horde","who lives at silverwind"},["q"]="Who controls Silverwind Refuge?"},{["a"]="It is located in south-central Ashenvale, positioned directly north of Mystral Lake and south of Iris Lake.",["al"]={"silverwind refuge location","where is silverwind refuge","how to get to silverwind"},["q"]="Where is Silverwind Refuge located?"},{["a"]="Travelers can find an inn, trade supply vendors, and professional trainers offering instruction in herbalism, alchemy, skinning, and hunter skills.",["al"]={"what is at silverwind refuge","silverwind refuge trainers","silverwind vendors"},["q"]="What services are found at the refuge?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","iris lake","mystral lake","night elf","sentinels","silverwind refuge"},["n"]="Silverwind Refuge",["s"]="Silverwind Refuge is a serene night elven settlement nestled in south-central Ashenvale, situated just north of Mystral Lake. Protected by Sentinels and allied water elementals, it offers a welcoming haven for travelers along the forest's wooded trails.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Resting between the placid waters of Mystral Lake and Iris Lake to the north, Silverwind Refuge stands as one of the major night elven waystations in central Ashenvale alongside Astranaar. It boasts a comfortable inn, craftsmen, and wilderness trainers who instruct travelers in herbalism, alchemy, skinning, and hunting. Guarded by stalwart Sentinels alongside local water spirits, the retreat serves as a peaceful rest stop for allies moving through the shaded ancient woods.",["t"]="A Forest Sanctuary"}}}}}
t["subzone:silverwing-grove"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,273,28.504.0,40.250.0,34.116.0,37.228.0,41.159.0",["h"]="01ea2f",["n"]="Claro Ala de Plata",["s"]="Claro Ala de Plata. Escondido en la zona centro-sur de Vallefresno, cerca del Lago Cielo Estrellado, Claro Ala de Plata sirve como punto de concentración para las Centinelas Ala de Plata. Desde esta hondonada fortificada, los guerreros elfos de la noche reúnen a las fuerzas de la Alianza para hacer retroceder a los leñadores del clan Grito de Guerra que arrasan el bosque. Oculto bajo el dosel esmeralda al suroeste de Avanzada Ala de Plata, Claro Ala de Plata es un puesto militar de concentración crucial para las Centinelas Ala de Plata. Lejos de ser un apacible retiro boscoso, funciona como el centro neurálgico de operaciones para la encarnizada disputa territorial de los elfos de la noche contra las talas de la Horda en Garganta Grito de Guerra. Oficiales de alto rango de la Alianza, suministros y exploradores se reúnen aquí, organizando escaramuzas y congregando campeones para defender el ancestral Vallefresno de la expansión de los orcos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The grove is the primary staging ground for Alliance champions seeking to muster and enter the bloody skirmishes of Warsong Gulch.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Silverwing Grove represents the steadfast resolve to halt the desecration of sacred trees at the axes of the Warsong Clan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Silverwing Grove serves as the staging base for the Silverwing Sentinels. It is where the night elf military and their Alliance allies organize efforts to contest the Warsong Clan's deforesting efforts and enter the ongoing conflict in Warsong Gulch.",["al"]={"why is silverwing grove here","what is silverwing grove","purpose of silverwing grove"},["q"]="What is the purpose of Silverwing Grove?"},{["a"]="It is located in south-central Ashenvale, situated southwest of Silverwing Outpost and just west of Fallen Sky Lake.",["al"]={"silverwing grove location","where is silverwing grove","how to find silverwing grove"},["q"]="Where is Silverwing Grove located?"},{["a"]="The grove is manned by the Silverwing Sentinels alongside Alliance military commanders, including an Alliance Brigadier General, logistical vendors, and officers such as Sentinel Farsong who coordinate efforts against the Horde.",["al"]={"who is at silverwing grove","silverwing grove npcs","who runs silverwing grove"},["q"]="Who operates out of Silverwing Grove?"},{["a"]="No. The grove is an active military post populated by hostile Alliance sentinels and guards who will immediately attack any encroaching Horde members on sight.",["al"]={"is silverwing grove hostile","can horde go to silverwing grove","horde silverwing grove"},["q"]="Can Horde players enter Silverwing Grove?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","fallen sky lake","sentinel farsong","silverwing grove","silverwing sentinels","warsong gulch"},["n"]="Silverwing Grove",["s"]="Tucked away in south-central Ashenvale near Fallen Sky Lake, Silverwing Grove serves as the staging grounds for the Silverwing Sentinels. From this fortified hollow, night elf warriors muster Alliance forces to push back the Warsong Clan loggers tearing through the forest.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Hidden beneath the emerald canopy southwest of Silverwing Outpost, Silverwing Grove is a crucial military staging post for the Silverwing Sentinels. Rather than a tranquil woodland retreat, it functions as the operational heartbeat for the night elves' bitter territorial contest against the Horde's lumber operations in Warsong Gulch. High-ranking Alliance officers, provisions, and scouts gather here, organizing skirmishes and marshaling champions to defend ancient Ashenvale against orcish expansion.",["t"]="Front Line of the Forest War"}}}}}
t["subzone:silverwing-outpost"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,248,21.501.0,18.384.1,36.150.0,32.142.0,55.217.0,33.213.0",["h"]="9d0eaa",["n"]="Avanzada Ala de Plata",["s"]="Avanzada Ala de Plata. La Avanzada Ala de Plata es una guarnición fortificada de elfos de la noche situada en el centro-sur de Vallefresno, al este del Río Falfarren. Comandada por Duriel Moonfire, se erige como el bastión más oriental de la Alianza frente a la Horda en este bosque en disputa. Situada al suroeste del Puesto del Hachazo y justo al norte de la frontera con Los Baldíos, la Avanzada Ala de Plata ocupa una posición estratégica intrínsecamente peligrosa. Al asentarse en la orilla oriental del Río Falfarren —un territorio fuertemente disputado y patrullado por la Horda—, la avanzada sirve como escudo directo para las posesiones de los elfos de la noche en las profundidades del bosque. Duriel Moonfire y sus Centinelas Ala de Plata permanecen bajo el asedio constante de los orcos cercanos, decididos a purgar por completo las fuerzas de los elfos de la noche de la zona.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Silverwing Outpost serves as your vital forward redoubt on the Horde side of the river, checking orc expansion out of Splintertree Post.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, the outpost is an intolerable thorn in the side of Splintertree Post, directly obstructing your movements and supply lines through southern Ashenvale."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is located in south-central Ashenvale, southwest of Splintertree Post, north of the Barrens border, and on the eastern side of the Falfarren River.",["al"]={"silverwing location","where is silverwing","silverwing outpost map"},["q"]="Where is Silverwing Outpost located?"},{["a"]="The outpost is commanded by Duriel Moonfire, a night elf officer leading the Silverwing Sentinels defending the eastern reaches of the forest.",["al"]={"silverwing leader","who leads silverwing outpost","duriel moonfire"},["q"]="Who commands Silverwing Outpost?"},{["a"]="Silverwing Outpost sits directly on the eastern side of the Falfarren River near Splintertree Post. Its presence allows the Sentinels to cut off Horde supply lines and directly threaten orcish operations in Ashenvale.",["al"]={"why attack silverwing","horde interest in silverwing","splintertree vs silverwing"},["q"]="Why does the Horde target this outpost so aggressively?"},{["a"]="The Silverwing Sentinels are a militant order of night elf warriors and huntresses dedicated to protecting Ashenvale from incursions, particularly against the encroaching lumber camps and war parties of the Horde.",["al"]={"what are silverwings","silverwing sentinels lore","silverwing faction"},["q"]="Who are the Silverwing Sentinels?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","duriel moonfire","falfarren river","silverwing outpost","silverwing sentinels","splintertree post","torek"},["n"]="Silverwing Outpost",["s"]="Silverwing Outpost is a fortified night elf garrison positioned in south-central Ashenvale, east of the Falfarren River. Commanded by Duriel Moonfire, it stands as the easternmost bastion of the Alliance against the Horde in the contested woodland.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated southwest of Splintertree Post and just north of the border with the Barrens, Silverwing Outpost holds an inherently perilous strategic position. By sitting on the eastern side of the Falfarren River—territory heavily contested and patrolled by the Horde—the outpost serves as a direct shield for night elf holdings deeper in the forest. Duriel Moonfire and her Silverwing Sentinels remain under constant siege from nearby orcs determined to purge night elf forces from the area entirely.",["t"]="East of the Falfarren"},{["b"]="The skirmishes surrounding Silverwing Outpost are among the fiercest in Ashenvale. Orcish war parties based out of Splintertree Post, such as raiders led by Torek, launch relentless ambushes against the garrison's walls. For the Horde, neutralizing the outpost is essential to securing the road and expanding resource operations without the constant threat of Sentinel counterattacks.",["t"]="The Constant Front"}}}}}
t["subzone:sishir-canyon"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,352,15.507.0,18.412.0,22.148.0,34.180.0,17.178.0,30.134.0",["h"]="a732d4",["n"]="Cañón Sishir",["s"]="Cañón Sishir. El Cañón Sishir es un escarpado desfiladero en Sierra Espolón, que se abre paso hacia el este a través de las abruptas cumbres. Plagado por densos enjambres de monstruosas arañas Musgoprofundo y cubierto de telarañas, sirve como peligroso acceso a las Ruinas de Eldre'thar. Los viajeros que se atreven a adentrarse en sus enmarañadas profundidades deben enfrentarse a arácnidos venenosos y a su amenazante matriarca. El Cañón Sishir, que nace como una bifurcación de los caminos de montaña de Sierra Espolón, es un traicionero corredor natural que se abre paso hacia las antiguas Ruinas de Eldre'thar. Lejos de ser un apacible sendero de montaña, el desfiladero ha sido completamente invadido por arañas Musgoprofundo. Sus pegajosos mantos de seda y sus cúmulos de sacos de huevos asfixian el suelo pedregoso y las paredes de roca, transformando el barranco en un nido viviente. Los viajeros y centinelas que buscan las ruinas de los elfos de la noche que aguardan más allá deben abrirse camino entre enjambres de agresivas tejedoras.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="The dangerous webbing and venomous Deepmoss spiders make Sishir Canyon a demanding testing ground for hunters tracking and trapping wild beasts in tight ravine quarters.",["race:NightElf"]="The overrun canyon cuts off easy, safe passage to the ancestral Ruins of Eldre'thar, requiring Kaldorei sentinels and scholars to fight through dense spider nests to reach their heritage."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Sishir Canyon is a spider-infested gorge in the Stonetalon Mountains that winds from the main mountain paths toward the ancient Ruins of Eldre'thar.",["al"]={"where is sishir canyon","sishir canyon location"},["q"]="What is Sishir Canyon?"},{["a"]="The canyon is thoroughly claimed by predatory Deepmoss spiders. The arachnids have coated the ravine in dense webbing and egg sacs, preying on anything that enters their territory.",["al"]={"monsters in sishir canyon","spiders in stonetalon canyon"},["q"]="What creatures live in the canyon?"},{["a"]="Besseleth is the formidable spider matriarch dwelling deep within Sishir Canyon. She leads the Deepmoss brood and poses the greatest threat to travelers passing through the area.",["al"]={"besseleth location","giant spider sishir canyon"},["q"]="Who is Besseleth?"},{["a"]="Following the canyon eastward leads directly out to the Ruins of Eldre'thar, an ancient night elven site tucked high in the mountains.",["al"]={"what is at the end of sishir canyon","path through sishir canyon"},["q"]="Where does Sishir Canyon lead?"}},["kw"]={"besseleth","deepmoss","eldre'thar","sishir canyon","spiders","stonetalon","webbing"},["n"]="Sishir Canyon",["s"]="Sishir Canyon is a rugged gorge in the Stonetalon Mountains, carving an eastward path through the craggy heights. Thickly swarmed by monstrous Deepmoss spiders and choked in webbing, it serves as the dangerous approach to the Ruins of Eldre'thar. Travelers who brave its tangled depths must contend with venomous arachnids and their brooding matriarch.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Branching off the mountain roads of the Stonetalon range, Sishir Canyon is a treacherous natural corridor cutting toward the ancient Ruins of Eldre'thar. Rather than a quiet mountain trail, the gorge has been thoroughly overrun by Deepmoss spiders. Their sticky silken sheets and clusters of egg sacs smother the stony ground and rock walls, transforming the ravine into a living nest. Travelers and sentinels seeking the night elven ruins beyond must cut their way through swarms of aggressive webspinners.",["t"]="The Webbed Pass"},{["b"]="Lurking in the deepest recess of the canyon is Besseleth, the massive and deadly matriarch of the Deepmoss brood. Her venom and monstrous size make her a terror to anyone attempting to secure the pass. Local forces in Stonetalon keep a wary watch on the canyon, warning adventurers that venturing into the webbed recesses means facing not just scattered spiders, but an apex predator fiercely guarding her brood.",["t"]="Besseleth's Domain"}}}}}
